WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:04:34.619 --> 00:04:42.619
Chapter One
Last Stage to Red Rock


00:05:12.357 --> 00:05:13.709
Got room for one more?


00:05:15.307 --> 00:05:20.347
Who the hell are you,
and what happened to them?


00:05:21.269 --> 00:05:23.800
Names Major Marquis Warren former U.S.
Calvary.


00:05:23.812 --> 00:05:25.879
Currentrly I'm a servant of the court.


00:05:25.999 --> 00:05:28.911
Tryin' to bringin' a coupla'
no-goods into market.


00:05:29.031 --> 00:05:31.103
I got paperwork on 'em in my pocket.


00:05:31.223 --> 00:05:33.010
You takin' 'em into Red Rock?


00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.284
I figure that's where you headed, right?


00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:42.133
That damblasted blizzards
been on our ass for the last three hours.


00:05:42.253 --> 00:05:45.432
Ain't no way we gonna make it all the
way to Red Rock 'fore it catches us.


00:05:45.552 --> 00:05:48.362
So ya' hightailin' it
halfway to Minnie's Haberdashery?


00:05:48.482 --> 00:05:50.308
You know I am.


00:05:50.428 --> 00:05:54.201
- May I come aboard?
- Well smoke...


00:05:54.321 --> 00:05:57.273
it up to me, yes.


00:05:57.622 --> 00:06:00.469
- But it ain't up to me.
- Who's it up to?


00:06:00.838 --> 00:06:02.661
Fella in the wagon.


00:06:02.989 --> 00:06:05.202
Fella' in the wagon
not partial to company?


00:06:05.322 --> 00:06:09.179
Fella' in the wagon he paid for a private
trip. And i'm here to tell ya'...


00:06:09.299 --> 00:06:11.565
he paid a pretty penny for privacy.


00:06:11.577 --> 00:06:14.424
So if you wanna' go
to Minnie's with us...


00:06:14.533 --> 00:06:17.119
- you gotta' talk to him.
- Well...


00:06:19.762 --> 00:06:20.832
that's what i'll do.


00:06:23.538 --> 00:06:25.137
Hold it black fella'!


00:06:26.207 --> 00:06:28.101
'fore you approach,


00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:32.509
you take them two guns of yours and
lay 'em on that rock over yonder.


00:06:33.231 --> 00:06:36.479
Then you raise both
your hands way above your hat.


00:06:37.858 --> 00:06:39.121
Then you approach....


00:06:40.153 --> 00:06:41.184
molasses-like.


00:06:42.447 --> 00:06:44.458
Real trustin' fella', huh?


00:06:44.578 --> 00:06:45.824
Not so much.


00:06:59.694 --> 00:07:00.701
Put 'em down.


00:07:09.858 --> 00:07:10.858
Come on ahead.


00:07:12.207 --> 00:07:14.714
I said way above your hat, god dammit.


00:07:16.984 --> 00:07:17.984
Now come forward.


00:07:19.764 --> 00:07:20.957
That's far enough.


00:07:27.629 --> 00:07:30.763
I'll be dogged, you black fella' i know.


00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.739
Col. Something Warren, right?


00:07:33.859 --> 00:07:36.191
Major Marquis Warren.


00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:37.829
I know you too.


00:07:38.537 --> 00:07:41.972
We shared a steak dinner
once upon a time in Chattanooga.


00:07:42.747 --> 00:07:44.412
You John Ruth, The Hangman.


00:07:44.726 --> 00:07:45.726
That be me.


00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:48.633
- How longs that been?
- Since that steak?


00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.570
Eight months.


00:07:51.885 --> 00:07:54.559
So why don't you explain to me...


00:07:54.679 --> 00:07:57.454
what an african bounty
hunter's doin' wanderin'


00:07:57.466 --> 00:08:00.079
around in the snow in
the middle of Wyoming.


00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:02.237
I'm tryin' to get a coupla'
of bounty's to Red Rock.


00:08:02.249 --> 00:08:03.292
So you still in business?


00:08:03.412 --> 00:08:04.957
You know I am.


00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.054
What happened to your horse?


00:08:07.174 --> 00:08:11.565
Circumstances caused us to take the long
way around. My horse couldn't make it.


00:08:13.033 --> 00:08:15.328
You don't know nothin'
about this filly here?


00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.590
Nope.


00:08:16.601 --> 00:08:18.356
Don't even know your name?


00:08:18.476 --> 00:08:19.476
Nope.


00:08:19.614 --> 00:08:23.010
Well I guess that makes
this one fortuitous wagon.


00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.989
I sure as hell hope so.


00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.149
Major Marquis Warren,
this here is Daisy Domergue.


00:08:30.233 --> 00:08:33.511
Domergue, to you, this is Maj.
Warren.


00:08:33.631 --> 00:08:34.783
Howdy nigger!


00:08:36.094 --> 00:08:37.837
She's a pepper, ain't she?


00:08:38.401 --> 00:08:40.699
Now girl, don't you know
darkee's don't like bein'


00:08:40.711 --> 00:08:42.885
called niggers no more.
They find it offensive.


00:08:43.005 --> 00:08:45.730
- I been called worse.
- Now that I can believe.


00:08:46.002 --> 00:08:48.335
- Heard of her?
- Should I?


00:08:48.755 --> 00:08:50.853
Well she ain't no John Wilkes Booth, but...


00:08:51.469 --> 00:08:54.065
maybe you might of heard
tell 'bout the price on her head.


00:08:54.185 --> 00:08:56.254
- How much?
- Ten thousand dollars.


00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.214
Damn, what she do?
Kill Lily Langtree?


00:09:00.334 --> 00:09:01.354
Not quite.


00:09:02.233 --> 00:09:04.540
Now that ten thousand's
practically in my pocket.


00:09:05.432 --> 00:09:08.389
It's why I ain't too anxious
to be handin' out rides.


00:09:08.401 --> 00:09:10.985
Especially to professionals
open for business.


00:09:11.105 --> 00:09:16.024
Well I certainly can appreciate that.
I ain't got no designs on her.


00:09:16.144 --> 00:09:18.417
One of my fella's over
there is worth four


00:09:18.429 --> 00:09:21.085
thousand, one's worth
three, and one's worth one.


00:09:21.317 --> 00:09:23.366
That's damn sure good enough for me.


00:09:24.049 --> 00:09:25.049
Well...


00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.619
Let me see their paperwork.


00:09:27.739 --> 00:09:29.849
Like I said, molasses-like.


00:09:39.206 --> 00:09:40.206
Back off.


00:10:09.084 --> 00:10:09.845
Look...


00:10:09.965 --> 00:10:14.284
I sure hate to interrupt y'all!
But we gtta' cold damn blizzard,


00:10:14.404 --> 00:10:17.681
hot on our asses we tryin'
to beat to shelter!


00:10:17.801 --> 00:10:19.223
I realize that!


00:10:19.343 --> 00:10:22.430
Now shut your mouth
and hold them damn horses while I think!


00:10:25.968 --> 00:10:27.695
Ok boy, we'll give it a try.


00:10:27.815 --> 00:10:31.214
But you leave those pistols
over yonder with the driver.


00:10:34.358 --> 00:10:36.752
You ain't really gonna'
let that nigger ridin' in


00:10:36.764 --> 00:10:39.218
here is ya'? I mean maybe
up there with O.B., but...


00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.431
How you like the sound
of them bells, bitch?


00:10:43.895 --> 00:10:45.468
They are real pretty, ain't they?


00:10:46.963 --> 00:10:49.075
You open up your trashy
mouth again, I'll knock


00:10:49.087 --> 00:10:50.946
out them front teeth for ya'.
You got it?


00:10:53.743 --> 00:10:54.743
Yeah.


00:10:54.993 --> 00:10:56.553
Let me hear you say: "I got it."


00:10:59.144 --> 00:11:00.807
I got it.


00:11:00.927 --> 00:11:04.815
Well, I'm gonna need some help tyin'
these fella's up on the roof.


00:11:05.511 --> 00:11:08.617
Give O.B. fifty dollars when
ya' get to Red Rock, and he'll help ya'.


00:11:08.737 --> 00:11:11.904
Well, I agree with O.B.
This storm's got me concerned.


00:11:12.024 --> 00:11:14.421
We get goin' a lot
quicker you help out too.


00:11:14.433 --> 00:11:16.944
Goddamit to hell, I'm
already regretting this!


00:11:17.693 --> 00:11:21.754
Now I can't likely help ya' tie fella's
to the roof with my wrist cuffed to hers.


00:11:21.874 --> 00:11:24.242
And my wrist is gonna'
stay cuffed to hers, and


00:11:24.254 --> 00:11:26.535
she ain't never gonna'
leave my goddamn side,


00:11:26.655 --> 00:11:30.389
until I personally put her in the
Red Rock jail! Now do you got that?


00:11:31.266 --> 00:11:32.799
- Yeah, I got it.
- Good.


00:12:28.842 --> 00:12:31.072
So what happend to your horse?


00:12:32.155 --> 00:12:33.702
He got old.


00:12:33.822 --> 00:12:35.584
I done had him for a bit.


00:12:37.426 --> 00:12:39.909
When the weather took a
turn for the worse, he


00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.286
done what he could, but
he couldn't make it.


00:12:43.613 --> 00:12:46.165
- That's too bad.
- Yes it is.


00:12:47.003 --> 00:12:50.238
Me an' ole Lash rode a
lotta' miles together.


00:12:50.358 --> 00:12:52.838
You could say he was my best friend...


00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:56.707
if I considered stupid animals firends,
which I don't.


00:12:56.816 --> 00:12:59.544
Never the less....
I'm gonna' miss 'em.


00:13:02.676 --> 00:13:04.019
Who's Daisy Domergue?


00:13:04.031 --> 00:13:06.801
A no damn good murdering
bitch, that's who.


00:13:08.541 --> 00:13:12.949
I can see you ain't got mixed emotions
'bout bringing a woman to a rope.


00:13:13.297 --> 00:13:15.218
If by woman, you mean her?


00:13:15.566 --> 00:13:18.646
No I do not have mixed emotions.


00:13:19.956 --> 00:13:21.778
So you takin' her into Red Rock to hang?


00:13:21.898 --> 00:13:24.584
- You bet.
- Gonna' wait to watch it?


00:13:24.704 --> 00:13:26.417
You know I am.


00:13:26.887 --> 00:13:29.808
I wanna' hear her neck
snap with my own two ears.


00:13:31.449 --> 00:13:33.726
You never wait to watch 'em hang?


00:13:34.477 --> 00:13:35.945
My bounties never hang,


00:13:36.292 --> 00:13:37.983
cause I never bring 'em in alive.


00:13:38.931 --> 00:13:39.443
Never?


00:13:39.921 --> 00:13:40.921
Never ever.


00:13:41.794 --> 00:13:43.777
We talked about this in Chattanooga.


00:13:43.897 --> 00:13:47.024
Bringing desperate men in alive,
is a good way to get yourself dead.


00:13:47.824 --> 00:13:50.365
Can't catch me sleepin'
if I don't close my eyes.


00:13:50.485 --> 00:13:51.787
I don't wanna' work that hard.


00:13:51.799 --> 00:13:53.730
No one said the job
was suppose to be easy.


00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.300
No one said
it was suppose to be that hard, nether.


00:13:56.977 --> 00:13:58.701
But that little lady,


00:13:59.056 --> 00:14:01.176
is why they call him "The Hangman".


00:14:01.296 --> 00:14:03.907
When the handbill says
Dead or Alive, the rest of


00:14:03.919 --> 00:14:06.594
us shoot ya' in the back
from up on top of a perch


00:14:06.714 --> 00:14:13.227
somewhere, bring ya' in dead over a saddle.
But when John Ruth The Hangman catches ya',


00:14:13.276 --> 00:14:15.710
you don't die by a bullet in the back.


00:14:16.617 --> 00:14:20.087
When The Hangman catches you...
you hang.


00:14:22.321 --> 00:14:24.160
You overrate 'em nigger.


00:14:24.721 --> 00:14:26.577
I'll give you he got guts.


00:14:26.697 --> 00:14:28.887
But in the brains department,


00:14:29.007 --> 00:14:33.449
he like a man who took a
high dive in a low well.


00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:37.928
Now Daisy,


00:14:38.048 --> 00:14:41.591
I want us to work out a
signal system of communication.


00:14:42.177 --> 00:14:44.618
When I elbow you real hard in the face...


00:14:45.344 --> 00:14:46.582
that means: Shut up.


00:14:47.778 --> 00:14:48.778
You got it?


00:14:50.303 --> 00:14:51.598
I got it.


00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:36.264
I...


00:16:36.384 --> 00:16:39.744
I know we only met each other once before.


00:16:39.864 --> 00:16:43.762
And I don't mean to unduly
imply intimacy. But...


00:16:43.882 --> 00:16:44.882
Well...


00:16:46.241 --> 00:16:48.097
You still got it?


00:16:48.217 --> 00:16:50.044
I still got, what?


00:16:51.114 --> 00:16:52.854
The Lincoln letter?


00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:55.239
Of course.


00:16:57.558 --> 00:16:59.157
Do you got it on you?


00:16:59.995 --> 00:17:00.995
Where?


00:17:01.155 --> 00:17:02.155
Right here.


00:17:04.557 --> 00:17:07.406
Look, I know you gotta'
be real careful with it and all.


00:17:07.526 --> 00:17:10.568
I can imagine you probably
don't like to take


00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.567
it in an'out of the
envelope all that often.


00:17:13.687 --> 00:17:15.216
But if you wouldn't mind,


00:17:15.336 --> 00:17:18.181
i'd sure appreciate seein' that again.


00:17:22.885 --> 00:17:23.885
You right,


00:17:23.907 --> 00:17:27.757
I don't like taking it in an'out
of the envelope that much.


00:17:27.877 --> 00:17:29.467
- Yeah.
- But...


00:17:29.587 --> 00:17:31.404
as your saving my life an' all,


00:17:33.286 --> 00:17:35.580
I suppose I could let you read it again.


00:18:18.256 --> 00:18:22.195
"Ole Mary Todd's callin',
so I guess it must be time for bed"


00:18:24.581 --> 00:18:26.295
Ole Mary Todd.


00:18:33.629 --> 00:18:34.789
That gets me.


00:18:35.937 --> 00:18:37.470
That gets me too.


00:18:40.023 --> 00:18:42.446
You know what this is, tramp?


00:18:43.245 --> 00:18:45.411
It's a letter from Lincoln.


00:18:45.531 --> 00:18:48.208
It's a letter from Lincoln to him.


00:18:49.226 --> 00:18:51.533
They shared a correspondence
during the war.


00:18:51.653 --> 00:18:56.405
They was pen pals.
This is just one of the letters.


00:18:59.293 --> 00:19:00.293
What the...


00:19:01.909 --> 00:19:02.909
O.B.


00:19:03.405 --> 00:19:04.062
Stop!


00:19:04.182 --> 00:19:06.137
Whoa, easy.


00:19:11.989 --> 00:19:13.832
Of all the stupid,


00:19:13.952 --> 00:19:16.500
like to rip my goddamn arm off!


00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.288
I didn't,


00:19:51.408 --> 00:19:54.036
drag her stikin' ass up
this goddamn mountain, just


00:19:54.048 --> 00:19:56.638
for you to break her neck
on the ouskirts of town.


00:19:56.758 --> 00:19:59.486
You the one handed her my goddamn letter.


00:19:59.606 --> 00:20:01.445
I didn't give it to her,
I gave it to you!


00:20:04.822 --> 00:20:07.323
That nigger like to bust my jaw.


00:20:09.618 --> 00:20:11.512
You ruin that letter of his,


00:20:11.632 --> 00:20:14.619
that niggers gonna' stomp your
ass to death. And when he do,


00:20:14.739 --> 00:20:17.815
I'm gonna sit back on that
wagon wheel watch and laugh.


00:20:19.865 --> 00:20:20.865
How is it?


00:20:21.167 --> 00:20:22.894
She didn't help it none.


00:20:23.014 --> 00:20:24.196
But it's alright.


00:20:24.931 --> 00:20:28.072
Is that the way niggers treat their ladies?


00:20:28.192 --> 00:20:32.354
You... ain't no goddamn... lady!


00:20:38.534 --> 00:20:39.759
Hey Mister Ruth?


00:20:40.326 --> 00:20:41.326
What?


00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:44.464
There's another fella' on foot,
up here on the road!


00:20:46.551 --> 00:20:47.551
What?


00:20:49.233 --> 00:20:53.061
I said, there's another fella' on foot,
up here on the road!


00:21:13.492 --> 00:21:16.272
Considering there's a blizzard goin' on,


00:21:16.392 --> 00:21:19.533
whole lotta' fellas walkin' around,
wouldn't you say, Major?


00:21:19.653 --> 00:21:22.515
Considerin I'm one half
of them fellas, yeah...


00:21:22.635 --> 00:21:24.203
seems to be a lot of 'em.


00:21:24.323 --> 00:21:26.988
This changes things, son.


00:21:28.058 --> 00:21:30.636
Eight thousand dollars a
lotta' money for a nigger.


00:21:31.663 --> 00:21:33.841
But with a partner,
eighteen's a whole lot better.


00:21:33.961 --> 00:21:36.973
You really think I'm
in cahoots wit' that fella'? Or her?


00:21:37.553 --> 00:21:40.441
- Put them on.
- I ain't wearin' handcuffs.


00:21:40.561 --> 00:21:44.333
You put those on or you can stop worryin'
about this whole thing, right now.


00:22:02.841 --> 00:22:07.494
Chapter Two
Son of a Gun


00:22:08.113 --> 00:22:10.439
Hand your weapons to the driver.


00:22:10.559 --> 00:22:12.037
Little jumpy, ain't you?


00:22:12.157 --> 00:22:14.345
Never mind the jokes, just do it.


00:22:15.531 --> 00:22:17.425
- If you say so.
- I do.


00:22:41.204 --> 00:22:42.204
Ok...


00:22:42.635 --> 00:22:43.795
I done did it.


00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:45.689
O.B.?
Ya' got 'em?


00:22:45.809 --> 00:22:47.945
- I got 'em!
- Ok fella',


00:22:48.757 --> 00:22:51.477
you keep holdin'
that lantern in that one hand,


00:22:51.597 --> 00:22:53.668
and you keep that other
hand where I can see it.


00:22:54.646 --> 00:22:57.005
Walk over there where I can
get a good look at cha'.


00:23:09.547 --> 00:23:13.259
I'll be a goddamn dog in the manger.


00:23:13.379 --> 00:23:15.346
Is that you Chris Mannix?


00:23:16.301 --> 00:23:18.427
I'm sorry friend,
do we know each other?


00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:19.289
Not quite.


00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:22.848
- You know this fella'?
- Only by reputation.


00:23:22.968 --> 00:23:24.898
Like I said friend,


00:23:25.018 --> 00:23:27.218
you got me at a bit of a disadvantage.


00:23:27.338 --> 00:23:30.634
Keepin' you at a disadvantage,
is a advantage I intend to keep.


00:23:31.098 --> 00:23:32.619
Whoever you are mister,


00:23:33.212 --> 00:23:37.156
you sure sound tough when you're talkin'
to a desperate man knee deep in snow.


00:23:38.509 --> 00:23:39.682
I don't want no trouble.


00:23:40.094 --> 00:23:42.917
I just wanna' ride.
I'm freezin to death.


00:23:43.523 --> 00:23:44.812
Who is this joker.


00:23:45.173 --> 00:23:47.880
You heard of the rebel
renegade Erskine Mannix?


00:23:49.821 --> 00:23:51.703
- Mannix's Marauders?
- That's them.


00:23:51.823 --> 00:23:55.119
The scourge of South
Carolina, Mannix Marauders.


00:23:55.239 --> 00:23:57.507
That's Erskine's youngest boy, Chris.


00:23:57.627 --> 00:23:59.878
What brings you in my path, Chris Mannix?


00:23:59.998 --> 00:24:01.722
Well Mr. Face,


00:24:01.842 --> 00:24:05.988
I was riding to Red Rock and my horse
stepped in a gopher hole in the snow,


00:24:06.108 --> 00:24:08.295
fucked up his leg,
an' had to put 'er down.


00:24:08.415 --> 00:24:09.819
You got business in Red Rock?


00:24:09.939 --> 00:24:11.623
- Yes I do.
- What?


00:24:11.997 --> 00:24:13.595
I'm the new sheriff.


00:24:13.715 --> 00:24:15.709
- Horseshit.
- 'fraid not.


00:24:15.829 --> 00:24:18.648
- Where is your star?
- Well I ain't the sheriff yet.


00:24:18.768 --> 00:24:22.180
Once I get there they swear me in,
but that ain't happened yet.


00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:23.965
And that's when you get your star.


00:24:23.977 --> 00:24:26.197
You got anything that
can back any of this up?


00:24:26.317 --> 00:24:28.453
Yeah.
When we get to Red Rock.


00:24:28.573 --> 00:24:31.778
And from the look of those
three frozen fuckers up there,


00:24:31.898 --> 00:24:34.387
I figure you're a bounty hunter
open for business.


00:24:34.507 --> 00:24:37.790
And I figure you're taking them three
dead bodies into Red Rock to get paid?


00:24:38.525 --> 00:24:39.762
Three dead.


00:24:39.882 --> 00:24:41.760
One alive.


00:24:42.095 --> 00:24:44.441
- Who's that?
- Daisy Domergue.


00:24:44.561 --> 00:24:46.707
Who the fuck is Daisy Domergue?


00:24:46.765 --> 00:24:50.654
Not a goddamn thing to nobody,
except me and the hangman.


00:24:50.774 --> 00:24:51.856
The Hangman?


00:24:55.045 --> 00:24:56.985
Well I'll be double dogged damned.


00:24:58.037 --> 00:25:00.710
- You're The Hangman, Bob Ruth.
- It's John.


00:25:00.968 --> 00:25:02.072
And you...


00:25:02.929 --> 00:25:04.580
your're the nigger with the head...


00:25:04.700 --> 00:25:06.489
Major Marquis.


00:25:06.954 --> 00:25:11.299
My lord, is that really the real head
of Major Marquis, lookin' at me now?


00:25:11.344 --> 00:25:13.921
Yeah it's really me and
it's really my head.


00:25:14.398 --> 00:25:17.739
What's goin' on, y'all havin'
a bounty hunters picnic?


00:25:18.123 --> 00:25:20.896
Never mind, you takin' in
them three dead bodies


00:25:21.016 --> 00:25:22.917
and her to Red Rock
to get paid, ain't ya'?


00:25:22.929 --> 00:25:23.566
Yeah.


00:25:23.686 --> 00:25:24.686
Well...


00:25:24.731 --> 00:25:29.126
the man is red Rock suppose
to pay you is me. The new sherrif.


00:25:29.708 --> 00:25:33.307
So if you wanna get paid,
you need to get me to Red Rock.


00:25:33.427 --> 00:25:36.310
Well execuse me for findin'
it hard to belive a


00:25:36.311 --> 00:25:39.374
town electin' you to do
anything except drop dead.


00:25:39.494 --> 00:25:43.119
So I'm suppose to freeze death,
'cause you find something hard to belive?


00:25:47.035 --> 00:25:49.061
No I suppose not.


00:25:53.911 --> 00:25:56.129
Put them on and come inside.


00:26:02.856 --> 00:26:03.856
No.


00:26:08.462 --> 00:26:11.068
- Then you'll freeze.
- Then you'll hang.


00:26:12.589 --> 00:26:13.647
How so?


00:26:13.767 --> 00:26:15.608
Driver!


00:26:15.728 --> 00:26:17.608
Could you come down here and join us?


00:26:18.059 --> 00:26:21.878
I gotta hold these horses
I can hear you just fine from up here.


00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:25.968
You heard me tell this fella'
I'm the new sheriff of Red Rock, right?


00:26:26.806 --> 00:26:27.806
Yeah.


00:26:28.186 --> 00:26:30.031
Red Rock is my town.


00:26:30.766 --> 00:26:34.533
And I'm gonna' enter my town
in bounty hunters chains? No Sir!


00:26:34.653 --> 00:26:38.468
Sorry bushwackers,
I ain't entering Red Rock that way.


00:26:38.588 --> 00:26:41.182
When you finally get to
Red Rock, you're going


00:26:41.194 --> 00:26:43.910
to realize every goddamn
thing I said was right.


00:26:44.030 --> 00:26:46.103
And I expect you, O.B.,


00:26:46.223 --> 00:26:48.720
to tell the townsfolk
of Red Rock that John


00:26:48.732 --> 00:26:51.298
Ruth, let their new
sheriff freeze to death.


00:26:51.418 --> 00:26:53.452
There ain't no bounty
on my head, bushwacker.


00:26:53.572 --> 00:26:56.397
You let me die, that's murder.


00:27:05.044 --> 00:27:06.681
Hold out your hands.


00:27:08.692 --> 00:27:09.692
O.B.


00:27:10.303 --> 00:27:12.301
Give the Major back his iron.


00:27:14.079 --> 00:27:16.227
One thing I know for sure,


00:27:16.347 --> 00:27:19.286
this nigger-hatin' son of a gun
ain't partnered up with you.


00:27:19.789 --> 00:27:20.789
Now...


00:27:20.850 --> 00:27:22.895
I'll help protect your eight thousand,


00:27:23.475 --> 00:27:25.344
you help me protect my ten,


00:27:25.937 --> 00:27:26.937
deal?


00:27:28.373 --> 00:27:33.787
Ain't love grand. Y'all wanna' lie on
the ground and make snow angels together?


00:27:44.808 --> 00:27:47.206
- Tell ya' what, Bob...
- The name's John.


00:27:47.326 --> 00:27:51.923
When we get to Red Rock, I'll buy you and
Major Marquis there dinner and booze.


00:27:52.043 --> 00:27:54.696
- May way of sayin' thanks.
- I don't drink...


00:27:54.816 --> 00:27:58.640
with rebel renegades,
and I damn sure don't break bread with 'em.


00:27:58.924 --> 00:28:00.599
Well Mr. Ruth,


00:28:00.973 --> 00:28:04.182
you sound like you got
a axe to grind against The Cause.


00:28:04.302 --> 00:28:06.489
The cause of a renegade army?


00:28:06.828 --> 00:28:10.373
A bunch of losers gone loco, you bet I do.


00:28:10.598 --> 00:28:14.615
Ya' wrapped yourselves up in the
Rebel Flag as an excuse to kill and steal.


00:28:14.735 --> 00:28:19.221
And this should interest you Warren,
imparticular emancipated blacks.


00:28:19.341 --> 00:28:21.547
Sounds like my kinda' fella'.


00:28:23.830 --> 00:28:28.831
Sounds to me you been readin' a lotta'
newspapers printed in Washington D.C.


00:28:29.867 --> 00:28:34.095
Anywho, I'm just tryin'
to let y'all know grateful I am.


00:28:34.559 --> 00:28:37.449
I was a goner, and y'all saved me.


00:28:37.461 --> 00:28:40.264
You wanna' show me how
grateful you are...


00:28:40.664 --> 00:28:41.664
shut up!


00:28:43.121 --> 00:28:45.995
God damnit, Daisy it's comin'.


00:28:49.102 --> 00:28:50.713
Here, last piece.


00:29:02.751 --> 00:29:04.878
Does he know how famous you once was?


00:29:06.064 --> 00:29:07.366
I don't think so.


00:29:09.570 --> 00:29:10.570
Black eye.


00:29:11.864 --> 00:29:13.888
Do you know who he is?


00:29:14.222 --> 00:29:16.408
Do I know about the thirty
thousand dollar reward


00:29:16.420 --> 00:29:18.618
the Confederacy put on the
head of Major Marquis?


00:29:20.736 --> 00:29:21.736
Yeah.


00:29:21.896 --> 00:29:24.316
Them hillbillies went nigger head hunting,


00:29:24.436 --> 00:29:26.627
but they never did
get 'em the right nigger head, did they?


00:29:26.747 --> 00:29:28.392
No they didn't.


00:29:28.512 --> 00:29:30.493
But it wasn't for lack of tryin'.


00:29:30.613 --> 00:29:35.323
Them peckawoods left their homes and their
families, and come to this snowy mountain,


00:29:35.443 --> 00:29:38.456
lookin' for me and fortune.


00:29:38.576 --> 00:29:40.157
None of them found fortune.


00:29:40.905 --> 00:29:43.096
The ones you ain't ever heard of no more,


00:29:44.063 --> 00:29:44.953
they found me.


00:29:44.965 --> 00:29:47.672
Now it didn't stay 30
thousand the length of the war.


00:29:47.792 --> 00:29:51.295
Once passions had colled,
it dropped down to eight, then five.


00:29:51.415 --> 00:29:54.221
But, I bet even
when it was five thousand,


00:29:54.341 --> 00:29:57.722
you had your share
of country boys comin' to call?


00:29:58.701 --> 00:30:00.067
You know I did.


00:30:00.699 --> 00:30:02.645
Why did they have a reward on you?


00:30:02.980 --> 00:30:06.499
The Confederates took exception
to my capacity for killing them.


00:30:06.860 --> 00:30:08.948
After I broke out of Wellenbeck,


00:30:09.308 --> 00:30:13.536
The South took my continued
existence as a personal affront.


00:30:13.878 --> 00:30:16.778
So The Cause put a reward on my head.


00:30:17.950 --> 00:30:19.033
What's...


00:30:19.858 --> 00:30:20.858
Wellenbeck?


00:30:20.958 --> 00:30:23.937
You ain't never heard of Wellenbeck
prisoner of war camp, West Virginia?


00:30:24.057 --> 00:30:26.051
No Reb, I ain't never heard of it!


00:30:26.940 --> 00:30:28.719
You bust out?


00:30:29.440 --> 00:30:32.250
Maj. Marquis did more than bust out.


00:30:33.036 --> 00:30:36.710
Maj. Marquis had a bright idea.
So bright...


00:30:37.083 --> 00:30:40.563
you got to wonder,
why nobody never thought about it before.


00:30:42.110 --> 00:30:44.236
Tell John Ruth about your bright idea.


00:30:46.530 --> 00:30:49.933
Well the whole damn place
was just made out of kindling.


00:30:51.609 --> 00:30:52.936
So I burnt it down.


00:30:59.472 --> 00:31:02.630
There was a rookie regiment
spendin' the overnight in that camp.


00:31:03.120 --> 00:31:06.522
47 men...
burnt to a crisp.


00:31:06.642 --> 00:31:09.230
Southern youth, farmer's sons...


00:31:09.462 --> 00:31:11.730
- Cream of the crop...
- And I say, "Let 'em burn".


00:31:12.362 --> 00:31:15.004
I'm suppose to apologize
for killin' Johnny Reb?


00:31:15.867 --> 00:31:18.690
You joined the war to
keep niggers in chains.


00:31:18.810 --> 00:31:21.409
I joined the war to kill White Southern


00:31:21.421 --> 00:31:24.490
Crackers And that means
kill 'em anyway I can.


00:31:25.236 --> 00:31:29.206
Shoot 'em. Stab 'em.
Drown 'em. Burn 'em.


00:31:29.326 --> 00:31:31.045
Drop a big ole' rock on their head.


00:31:31.165 --> 00:31:34.679
Whatever it took to put
White Southern Crackers in the ground


00:31:34.799 --> 00:31:37.867
that's what I joined the war to do,
and that's what I did.


00:31:37.987 --> 00:31:39.826
To answer your question, John Ruth,


00:31:39.946 --> 00:31:44.569
when Major Marquis
burned forty seven men alive,


00:31:44.689 --> 00:31:47.443
for no more a reason then to give
a nigger a run for the trees,


00:31:47.563 --> 00:31:50.188
that's when The South put a reward
on the head of Major Marquis.


00:31:50.308 --> 00:31:52.082
And I made them trees, Mannix.


00:31:52.202 --> 00:31:55.820
And you best belive I ain't look back
till I crossed The Northern Line.


00:31:55.940 --> 00:31:59.958
But you had a surprise waitin' for you
on The Northern Side, didn't ya'?


00:32:00.294 --> 00:32:04.483
See once they started pullin' out
all the burnt bodies at Wellenbeck,


00:32:04.603 --> 00:32:07.757
seems not all of them boys were Rebs.


00:32:07.877 --> 00:32:11.431
You burnt up some of your own boys,
didn't ya' Major?


00:32:11.551 --> 00:32:13.932
How many burnt prisoners
they end up findin'?


00:32:14.052 --> 00:32:17.631
Wasn't the final Yankee death count
somethin' like 37?


00:32:20.019 --> 00:32:22.374
That's the thing about war Mannix,


00:32:22.494 --> 00:32:23.494
people die.


00:32:24.724 --> 00:32:27.921
So ya' chalkin' it up to "War Is Hell", ha?


00:32:28.424 --> 00:32:32.471
Well admittedly that's a hard argument
to argue with. But if memory serves,


00:32:32.754 --> 00:32:36.054
your side didn't look at it that way.


00:32:36.300 --> 00:32:41.340
I think they thought,
37 white men for one nigger


00:32:41.460 --> 00:32:43.325
wasn't so hot a trade.


00:32:43.445 --> 00:32:46.562
I belive they accused you


00:32:46.682 --> 00:32:50.696
of being a kill crazy nigger who
only joined the war to kill white folks


00:32:50.816 --> 00:32:54.070
and the whole Blue and Grey
of it all didn't really much matter to ya'.


00:32:54.190 --> 00:32:57.066
And that's why they drummed
your black ass outta'


00:32:57.078 --> 00:32:59.908
the Cavalry with a yellow
stripe down your back.


00:33:00.514 --> 00:33:02.473
Isn't it Major?


00:33:02.593 --> 00:33:03.775
Horse shit.


00:33:04.511 --> 00:33:07.398
If he did all that, the
Cavalry woulda' shot him.


00:33:07.518 --> 00:33:09.550
I didn't say they could prove it.


00:33:09.670 --> 00:33:12.618
But they sure did think it out loud,
didn't they Major?


00:33:13.817 --> 00:33:14.817
But,


00:33:14.878 --> 00:33:20.030
Warren's war record was stellar,
and that's what saved his ass.


00:33:20.825 --> 00:33:23.647
Are you killed yourself your share of


00:33:23.659 --> 00:33:27.089
redskins in your day,
didn't ya' Black Major?


00:33:27.209 --> 00:33:29.551
Cavalry tends to look kindly on that.


00:33:29.563 --> 00:33:32.800
I'll tell a' what The Cavalry
didn't look kindly on.


00:33:33.110 --> 00:33:35.572
Mannix's Marauders that's what.


00:33:35.856 --> 00:33:38.072
And the fact that Erskine
Mannix's little boy


00:33:38.084 --> 00:33:40.070
would talk about anybody else's behavior


00:33:40.190 --> 00:33:44.399
during war time makes
me wanna horse laugh.


00:33:44.519 --> 00:33:47.067
Don't you say anything about my daddy,


00:33:48.059 --> 00:33:49.516
what he fought for,


00:33:49.636 --> 00:33:54.014
was dignity in defeat,
and against the unconditional surrender.


00:33:54.134 --> 00:33:58.061
We weren't foreign barbatians
pounding on the city walls.


00:33:58.181 --> 00:34:00.356
We were your brothers.


00:34:01.323 --> 00:34:03.707
- We deserved dignity in defeat.
- Just,


00:34:03.827 --> 00:34:08.296
how many nigger towns did y'all sack
in your fight for dignity in defeat?


00:34:08.416 --> 00:34:11.286
My faire share, Black Major.


00:34:11.406 --> 00:34:15.668
'Cuz when niggers are scared,
that's when white folks are safe.


00:34:18.220 --> 00:34:20.785
You gonna talk that hateful nigger talk,


00:34:20.905 --> 00:34:22.886
you ride up top wtih O.B.


00:34:24.434 --> 00:34:29.551
No no no, you got me talkin' politics


00:34:29.671 --> 00:34:31.111
I didn't wanna'.


00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:34.849
Like I said y'all,
I'm just happy to be alive.


00:34:37.337 --> 00:34:38.337
I...


00:34:38.948 --> 00:34:41.745
I think I'll just look out this winda'


00:34:42.930 --> 00:34:45.908
let this beatuiful
carriage rock me to sleep.


00:34:46.926 --> 00:34:48.950
And dream about how lucky I am.


00:35:03.991 --> 00:35:07.987
Chapter Three
Minnie's Haberdashery


00:35:53.669 --> 00:35:54.878
Get in there.


00:35:58.761 --> 00:35:59.761
Easy.


00:36:24.959 --> 00:36:26.772
What the hell's going on,


00:36:26.892 --> 00:36:29.760
we weren't expecting another stage tonight?


00:36:29.880 --> 00:36:33.514
I can see
you already got another one up in here.


00:36:33.634 --> 00:36:36.624
I just got through putting the horses away.


00:36:36.744 --> 00:36:41.151
This ain't the normal line. But we are
stuck on the wrong side of a blizzard,


00:36:41.271 --> 00:36:45.904
so it looks like you're stuck with us.
Are Minnie and Sweet Dave inside?


00:36:46.371 --> 00:36:49.932
They ain't here.
I'm running the place while they're gone.


00:36:51.785 --> 00:36:54.008
Where's Minnie and Sweet Dave?


00:36:54.362 --> 00:36:58.632
He says they ain't here. He's lookin'
after the place while they gone.


00:36:58.752 --> 00:37:00.323
Who are you?


00:37:02.627 --> 00:37:03.997
I'm Bob.


00:37:06.349 --> 00:37:09.878
Well whoever you are,
help O.B. with the horses.


00:37:12.440 --> 00:37:16.936
Get 'em outta this cold,
before that blizzard hit's 'em.


00:37:21.084 --> 00:37:25.845
I just put those other horses away.
You need it done fast, you need to help.


00:37:26.441 --> 00:37:28.874
I got two of my best men on it.


00:37:30.550 --> 00:37:33.579
You heard him freeloaders, get to work.


00:37:37.243 --> 00:37:38.541
Come on let's go!


00:37:39.604 --> 00:37:42.053
- Open up!
- Kick it open!


00:37:42.173 --> 00:37:44.309
- What?
- Kick it open!


00:37:46.098 --> 00:37:49.336
Shut that door,
there's a goddamn blizzard out there!


00:37:49.456 --> 00:37:52.688
- You gotta' nail it shut!
- You have to nail it shut!


00:37:53.622 --> 00:37:56.950
- Hold it shut!
- There's a hammer and nails by the door!


00:37:57.070 --> 00:38:01.307
You have to nail it shut!
There's a hammer and nails by the door!


00:38:01.935 --> 00:38:03.868
- Give me a hammer.
- Yeah.


00:38:12.632 --> 00:38:16.128
You need to do two pieces of wood!
One ain't good enough!


00:38:16.248 --> 00:38:19.754
- Two pieces of wood.
- That fuckin' thing is busted!


00:38:19.874 --> 00:38:22.895
Not just one piece of wood.


00:38:23.015 --> 00:38:26.037
- Gimme that other piece of wood.
- Yeah, allright.


00:38:30.388 --> 00:38:32.482
- Gimme the nail.
- Here.


00:38:45.582 --> 00:38:46.582
Jesus.


00:38:50.320 --> 00:38:52.543
That door's a son of a gun.


00:38:52.663 --> 00:38:55.427
Who's the idiot who broke that,
that Mexican fella'?


00:38:55.894 --> 00:38:57.183
Good heavens,


00:38:57.457 --> 00:38:58.810
a woman


00:38:58.930 --> 00:39:02.919
out in this white hell.
You must be frozen solid, poor thing.


00:39:05.465 --> 00:39:08.526
Looks like Minnie's got her a full house.


00:39:10.702 --> 00:39:12.957
When did you fella's arrive?


00:39:13.972 --> 00:39:16.486
About forty minutes ago.


00:39:17.001 --> 00:39:19.549
The Cowboy fella' in the
courner, is that your driver?


00:39:19.561 --> 00:39:20.594
No he's a passenger.


00:39:20.714 --> 00:39:23.598
The driver lit out. He
said he was going to


00:39:23.610 --> 00:39:26.572
spend the blizzard shacked
up with a friend.


00:39:27.687 --> 00:39:30.536
Jesus Christ, that's awful!


00:39:31.293 --> 00:39:36.174
Christ almighty, what that Mexican fella'
do, soak his ole socks in the pot?


00:39:36.432 --> 00:39:41.169
I think we all felt the same way, but were
a little too polite to say something.


00:39:41.289 --> 00:39:45.310
- He don't have that problem.
- Where's the well water?


00:39:45.680 --> 00:39:47.291
Over there.


00:39:53.103 --> 00:39:54.103
So,


00:39:54.206 --> 00:39:59.432
all three of you fellas' headed to Red
Rock, when the blizzard stopped ya', huh?


00:39:59.552 --> 00:40:03.463
Yes, all three of us
were on that stagecouch out there.


00:40:15.547 --> 00:40:16.772
Coffybeans?


00:40:18.738 --> 00:40:19.898
Over there.


00:40:27.631 --> 00:40:29.242
Get your hand outta' there.


00:40:33.657 --> 00:40:36.688
The new sheriff of Red
Rock is traveling with us.


00:40:36.700 --> 00:40:39.216
Sheriff of Red Rock, that'll be the day.


00:40:39.474 --> 00:40:42.302
If he is a goddamn sheriff,
I'm a monkey's uncle.


00:40:42.314 --> 00:40:43.260
Good.


00:40:43.380 --> 00:40:46.949
Then you can share bananas
with your nigger friend in the stable.


00:40:47.069 --> 00:40:48.069
So...


00:40:48.770 --> 00:40:51.501
the new sheriff of Red
Rock is traveling with you?


00:40:51.513 --> 00:40:52.427
No he's lyin'


00:40:52.686 --> 00:40:55.054
he ain't sheriff of nothin'


00:40:55.174 --> 00:41:00.403
He's a southern renegade. He's just talkin'
his self outta' freezin' to death, is all.


00:41:00.523 --> 00:41:02.779
What the fuck I tell you
about talkin', huh?


00:41:02.899 --> 00:41:06.154
I'll bust you in the mouth right in
front of these people, I don't give a fuck!


00:41:06.274 --> 00:41:08.474
You never gave your name, sir.


00:41:08.594 --> 00:41:10.423
John Ruth.


00:41:10.543 --> 00:41:13.258
- Are you a lawman?
- I'm takin' her to the law.


00:41:13.378 --> 00:41:16.094
- You're a bounty hunter?
- That's right, Buster.


00:41:19.704 --> 00:41:22.443
- Do you have a warrant?
- 'Course I do.


00:41:22.700 --> 00:41:24.134
May I see it?


00:41:27.421 --> 00:41:28.421
Why?


00:41:29.628 --> 00:41:33.447
You're suppose to produce it upon request.
How am I suppose to know,


00:41:33.567 --> 00:41:35.332
you're not a villain,


00:41:35.452 --> 00:41:38.683
kidnapping this woman
without a warrant in your possession?


00:41:41.293 --> 00:41:42.872
What's your name, Buster?


00:41:43.645 --> 00:41:44.789
Well...


00:41:45.176 --> 00:41:47.560
it certainly isn't Buster.


00:41:48.237 --> 00:41:51.556
It's Oswaldo Mobray.


00:41:53.054 --> 00:41:55.568
- Oswaldo?
- Yes.


00:41:57.211 --> 00:41:58.275
Well...


00:41:59.225 --> 00:42:02.190
I got my warrant, Oswaldo.


00:42:15.718 --> 00:42:18.183
- I take it you're Daisy Domergue?
- Yeah it's her.


00:42:24.756 --> 00:42:28.381
- It says here, Dead or Alive?
- Yeah it does.


00:42:29.445 --> 00:42:33.505
Transporting a desperate
hostile prisoner such as her


00:42:33.773 --> 00:42:38.809
sounds like hard work.
Wouldn't transporting her be easier


00:42:38.929 --> 00:42:40.070
if she were dead?


00:42:40.082 --> 00:42:42.933
No one said the job
was suppose to be easy.


00:42:43.053 --> 00:42:45.244
And why is her hanging proper,
so important to you?


00:42:45.364 --> 00:42:49.410
Let's just say I don't like to cheat the
hangman. He's gotta' make a living too.


00:42:49.530 --> 00:42:51.270
Well I appreciate that.


00:42:52.188 --> 00:42:56.619
Allow me to properly introduce myself.


00:42:56.739 --> 00:42:59.035
I'm Oswaldo Mobray,


00:42:59.155 --> 00:43:01.484
The Hangman in these parts.


00:43:08.380 --> 00:43:11.168
- Looks like I brought you a customer.
- So it would appear.


00:43:11.288 --> 00:43:16.122
Have you ever spent two days or more
locked up with one of your customers?


00:43:16.242 --> 00:43:17.189
No I can't say I have.


00:43:17.201 --> 00:43:20.079
Don't talk to my prisoner. I talk to
my prisoner, that's it. You got it?


00:43:20.199 --> 00:43:22.284
I got I got. Jolly good.


00:43:22.404 --> 00:43:26.279
You got anything in here besides
coffee that can help warm us up?


00:43:26.399 --> 00:43:29.570
The Bar is open, follow moi.


00:44:28.585 --> 00:44:29.732
All right.


00:44:30.995 --> 00:44:31.995
All right.


00:44:32.108 --> 00:44:34.224
Come on, goddamnit I'm cold!


00:44:40.913 --> 00:44:45.528
I'll feed and water the horses.
You go inside and get some hot coffy.


00:44:46.056 --> 00:44:49.193
I've got some stew cooking.
Should be done soon.


00:44:49.205 --> 00:44:50.254
Now look...


00:44:50.374 --> 00:44:53.399
now matter how bad this blizzard gets,


00:44:53.519 --> 00:44:58.683
we still gotta' feed these horses
and take a squat from time to time.


00:44:58.803 --> 00:45:01.739
So me an' Chris better lay out a line


00:45:01.859 --> 00:45:05.970
from the stable to the front door,
and from the front door to the shithouse.


00:45:07.427 --> 00:45:08.427
Ok?


00:45:11.836 --> 00:45:12.880
Good idea.


00:45:14.646 --> 00:45:16.064
Come on, Chris.


00:45:18.397 --> 00:45:19.814
I'll give you a hand.


00:45:21.052 --> 00:45:23.423
No no no, go inside, get warm.


00:45:23.656 --> 00:45:27.680
You're doing stable work in a goddamn
blizzard, I offer to help and you say no?


00:45:29.326 --> 00:45:30.735
You're right, mi amigo.


00:45:31.637 --> 00:45:32.637
Muchas gracias.


00:45:35.384 --> 00:45:37.072
All right, follow me.


00:45:48.160 --> 00:45:51.369
We gonna' drop one, every ten paces.


00:45:51.691 --> 00:45:53.348
- From here to the door.
- Yeah!


00:45:53.360 --> 00:45:54.242
All right.


00:46:55.258 --> 00:46:59.543
Now, you're wanted for murder.


00:46:59.663 --> 00:47:02.862
For the sake of my analogy,
let's just assume that you did it.


00:47:02.982 --> 00:47:06.970
John Ruth wants to take you back to
Red Rock to stand trail for murder.


00:47:07.090 --> 00:47:10.853
And, if...
you're found guilty,


00:47:10.973 --> 00:47:15.082
the people of Red Rock will
hang you in the town square.


00:47:15.094 --> 00:47:16.535
And as the hangman,


00:47:16.644 --> 00:47:18.683
I will perform the execution.


00:47:19.842 --> 00:47:24.177
And if all those things
end up taking place,


00:47:24.297 --> 00:47:29.154
that's what civilized
society calls "justice".


00:47:30.974 --> 00:47:32.296
However,


00:47:33.053 --> 00:47:36.584
if the relatives and the
loved ones of the person


00:47:36.596 --> 00:47:39.926
you murdered were outside
that door right now.


00:47:40.046 --> 00:47:44.231
And after busting down that
door, they drug you out


00:47:44.243 --> 00:47:48.037
in the snow and hung you
up by the neck, that,


00:47:48.157 --> 00:47:50.720
we would be frontier justice.


00:47:50.840 --> 00:47:53.402
Now the good part


00:47:53.522 --> 00:47:58.590
about frontier justice is
it's very thirst quenching.


00:47:58.896 --> 00:48:03.408
The bad part is
it's apt to be Wrong as Right.


00:48:03.528 --> 00:48:06.371
Not in your case. In
your case, you'd have it


00:48:06.383 --> 00:48:09.176
comin'. But other people,
maybe not so much.


00:48:09.296 --> 00:48:13.754
But ultimately what's the
real difference between the two?


00:48:13.874 --> 00:48:19.312
The real difference is Me...
The Hangman.


00:48:19.432 --> 00:48:22.087
To me, it dosen't matter what you did.
When I hang you, I


00:48:22.099 --> 00:48:24.628
will get no satisfaction from your death.
It's my job.


00:48:24.748 --> 00:48:30.590
I hang you in red Rock, I move on to the
next town, I hang someone else there.


00:48:31.652 --> 00:48:34.262
The man who pulls the lever,


00:48:34.382 --> 00:48:38.548
that breaks your neck
will be a dispassionate man.


00:48:39.079 --> 00:48:42.727
And that dispassion is
the very essence of


00:48:42.739 --> 00:48:47.079
justice. For justice delivered
without dispassion,


00:48:47.329 --> 00:48:52.549
is always in danger of not being justice.


00:48:52.669 --> 00:48:53.871
Amen.


00:49:19.198 --> 00:49:22.711
No offense cowboy fella',
just gettin' your attention.


00:49:23.773 --> 00:49:26.012
Yeah, well...


00:49:26.625 --> 00:49:28.574
you got it.


00:49:28.945 --> 00:49:31.007
What'cha writing firend?


00:49:32.473 --> 00:49:35.151
Only thing I'm qualified to write about.


00:49:35.163 --> 00:49:36.367
What's that?


00:49:36.630 --> 00:49:38.515
My life story.


00:49:38.635 --> 00:49:42.059
- You're writing your life story?
- You bet I am.


00:49:42.317 --> 00:49:43.654
Am I in it?


00:49:45.829 --> 00:49:47.972
You just entered.


00:49:48.520 --> 00:49:50.724
Well you like writing
stories so much, why don't


00:49:50.736 --> 00:49:52.725
you tell me the story
that brings you here?


00:49:54.529 --> 00:49:56.366
- Who's askin'?
- I am.


00:49:56.486 --> 00:49:59.926
John Ruth. I'm bringin' in
this one to Red Rock to hang.


00:50:00.046 --> 00:50:02.289
Ain't no way I'm spendin'
a coupla' nights under a


00:50:02.301 --> 00:50:04.511
roof with somebody I don't
know who you they are.


00:50:04.631 --> 00:50:07.096
And I don't know who you are.
So...


00:50:07.216 --> 00:50:08.997
who are you?


00:50:09.286 --> 00:50:11.010
- Joe Gage.
- What?


00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:13.620
That's my name, Joe Gage.


00:50:13.740 --> 00:50:17.406
Ok Joe Gage, why you goin' to Red Rock?


00:50:17.526 --> 00:50:20.628
- I ain't goin' to Red Rock.
- Where you goin'?


00:50:21.304 --> 00:50:24.526
- About nine miles outside of Red Rock.
- What's there?


00:50:24.646 --> 00:50:25.783
My mother.


00:50:27.249 --> 00:50:28.538
Your mother?


00:50:29.005 --> 00:50:31.761
Listen, I'm just a cow puncher I just...


00:50:32.469 --> 00:50:35.128
I got back from a long drive and...


00:50:35.248 --> 00:50:38.028
I wasn't just an ass in a saddle
this time...


00:50:39.591 --> 00:50:41.348
I was a partner.


00:50:42.250 --> 00:50:44.232
For the first time in my life I,


00:50:44.699 --> 00:50:46.987
made a pretty penny and, eh....


00:50:49.257 --> 00:50:53.110
Come home and spend time with
my mother for Christmas.


00:50:53.979 --> 00:50:56.235
Now that's funny.


00:50:56.944 --> 00:51:00.086
'Cuz you don't look like the
coming home for Christmas type.


00:51:00.206 --> 00:51:02.045
Yeah, well...


00:51:03.898 --> 00:51:07.701
you know, looks can be deceiving.


00:51:08.280 --> 00:51:11.051
Because I definitely am a...


00:51:11.889 --> 00:51:15.466
coming home for Christmas to
spend time with mother type.


00:51:17.448 --> 00:51:19.527
Christmas with Mother?
I mean...


00:51:21.202 --> 00:51:22.926
it's a wonderful thing.


00:51:24.827 --> 00:51:29.193
Now is that... good
enough for you?


00:51:29.313 --> 00:51:30.579
John Ruth?


00:51:33.350 --> 00:51:34.510
For now.


00:51:35.895 --> 00:51:38.038
Just steer clear of my prisoner.


00:51:42.050 --> 00:51:44.016
Hello old timer.


00:51:45.682 --> 00:51:47.012
General.


00:51:48.527 --> 00:51:49.703
General.


00:51:51.443 --> 00:51:52.797
You sir,


00:51:53.667 --> 00:51:55.294
are a Hyena.


00:51:56.985 --> 00:51:59.176
And I have no wish to speak to you.


00:52:03.784 --> 00:52:05.588
I've been called worse.


00:52:08.778 --> 00:52:10.663
Fair enough, General.


00:52:11.437 --> 00:52:12.758
Sorry to bother you.


00:52:17.011 --> 00:52:18.651
- You gonna' kick it open.
- Kick it open.


00:52:29.836 --> 00:52:31.302
It's already cold enough in here.


00:52:37.329 --> 00:52:38.670
It dosen't have latch you
gonna' hammer up a board.


00:52:38.682 --> 00:52:39.359
You gotta' nail it shut!


00:52:39.479 --> 00:52:43.483
- The hammer and nails is by the door.
- There is a hammer and nails right there!


00:52:43.603 --> 00:52:44.971
Oh god,


00:52:46.329 --> 00:52:48.483
- Holdin' this Chris.
- Here, here.


00:52:57.426 --> 00:52:59.134
You need to nail it in!


00:53:02.727 --> 00:53:05.773
You need two pieces of wood.
You gotta' hammer another one.


00:53:06.417 --> 00:53:09.027
One ain't good enough!
It's gonna' blow right open.


00:53:09.800 --> 00:53:12.394
- Goddamn it!
- It's gotta' open if you don't.


00:53:12.514 --> 00:53:15.993
- Shut up!
- I got it! Son of a bitch!


00:53:28.414 --> 00:53:31.282
Jesis Christ, that door's a whore!


00:53:36.197 --> 00:53:37.985
I get it, haberdashery,


00:53:38.790 --> 00:53:40.427
that was a joke.


00:53:40.547 --> 00:53:42.093
How's the coffy?


00:53:42.213 --> 00:53:45.460
Now, pretty good, if I do say so myself.


00:53:48.490 --> 00:53:49.490
Thank you.


00:54:07.131 --> 00:54:09.500
Guess who he is?


00:54:11.143 --> 00:54:12.593
Buffalo Bill?


00:54:13.721 --> 00:54:15.606
Hardly, no.


00:54:15.864 --> 00:54:20.601
- I'm Oswaldo Mobray, I'm The...
- He's the hangman of Red Rock.


00:54:22.115 --> 00:54:24.000
- Oh, you are?
- Yes I am.


00:54:24.120 --> 00:54:28.607
Well good to meet you Mr.?


00:54:28.727 --> 00:54:31.975
- Mobray.
- Mobray, I'm Chris Mannix,


00:54:32.095 --> 00:54:34.166
- the new sheriff in Red Rock.
- Really?


00:54:34.286 --> 00:54:35.761
Horseshit!


00:54:35.881 --> 00:54:38.629
- Pay no attention to him.
- Horseshit!


00:54:38.749 --> 00:54:42.656
Fella' warmin' himself by the that pot
by the stove is a hell of driver named O.B.


00:54:42.776 --> 00:54:45.444
That's the only thing you
said that's the truth.


00:54:47.119 --> 00:54:49.173
You comin' into Red Rock
to hang Lance Lawson?


00:54:49.185 --> 00:54:49.874
Precisely.


00:54:49.994 --> 00:54:52.323
- Do you have the execution orders on you?
- In my beg.


00:54:52.443 --> 00:54:54.257
- May I see 'em?
- Of course.


00:55:00.073 --> 00:55:02.957
Who's Lance Lawson?


00:55:03.077 --> 00:55:06.227
He's a fell' been sittin' in the
Red Rock jail about a month now.


00:55:06.347 --> 00:55:11.221
He's the fella, who shot the fella',
who was sheriff 'fore me.


00:55:11.341 --> 00:55:12.962
Precisely.


00:55:23.322 --> 00:55:25.463
What did she mean when she said,


00:55:25.583 --> 00:55:27.946
bounty hunter's nigger
friend in the stable?


00:55:28.735 --> 00:55:31.055
He's got a nigger
bounty hunter firend in the stable.


00:55:32.264 --> 00:55:34.121
But all that just to guard her?


00:55:34.133 --> 00:55:36.936
I don't think that was
the original idea, but...


00:55:37.355 --> 00:55:39.788
that's the idea now.


00:55:40.110 --> 00:55:43.123
- Want a lil' snakebite in your coffy?
- Yeah.


00:55:44.526 --> 00:55:45.911
Five of you?


00:55:46.411 --> 00:55:48.561
Well, well, well, looks
like Minnie's Haberdashery


00:55:48.573 --> 00:55:50.438
is about to get cozy
for the next few days.


00:55:50.558 --> 00:55:51.985
Yes it does.


00:56:01.195 --> 00:56:03.056
Who's the chap with the Lincoln letter?


00:56:05.037 --> 00:56:06.552
The Lincoln what?


00:56:07.051 --> 00:56:09.081
The letter from Abraham Lincoln?


00:56:10.016 --> 00:56:12.723
President Abraham Lincoln?


00:56:13.399 --> 00:56:16.702
- Weren't you pen pals?
- With the President?


00:56:17.605 --> 00:56:20.569
I'm sorry, I heard somebody
in your party had a


00:56:20.581 --> 00:56:23.743
letter from Abraham Lincoln,
I assumed it was you.


00:56:23.863 --> 00:56:25.387
Not him!


00:56:25.507 --> 00:56:27.997
The black fella' in the stable.


00:56:28.117 --> 00:56:33.233
The nigger in the stable
has a letter from Abraham Lincoln?


00:56:33.652 --> 00:56:34.861
Yeah.


00:56:34.981 --> 00:56:39.356
The nigger in the stable
has a letter from Abraham Lincoln?


00:56:54.760 --> 00:56:56.436
Say your name was again?


00:56:57.193 --> 00:56:59.304
- Bob.
- Warren.


00:56:59.424 --> 00:57:01.205
Minnie and Sweet Dave in there?


00:57:01.325 --> 00:57:05.531
Minnie and Sweet Dave went to visit her
mother on the north side of the mountain.


00:57:05.651 --> 00:57:07.134
- What?
- Yeah.


00:57:07.254 --> 00:57:11.243
- They ain't here?
- Yes, they're visiting her mother.


00:57:11.363 --> 00:57:12.709
- Her mother?
- Yes.


00:57:16.592 --> 00:57:18.397
I never knew Minnie had a mother.


00:57:21.942 --> 00:57:23.972
Everybody's got a mother.


00:57:25.389 --> 00:57:26.855
Yeah, I suppose.


00:57:29.529 --> 00:57:33.187
- And she left you in charge?
- Si.


00:57:36.200 --> 00:57:38.375
That sure don't sound like Minnie.


00:57:39.761 --> 00:57:41.743
Are you callin' me a liar?


00:57:43.515 --> 00:57:45.094
Not yet, I ain't.


00:57:46.528 --> 00:57:49.927
- But it sounds peculiar, though,
- What sound peculiar?


00:57:50.443 --> 00:57:54.535
Well first of, Minnie never struck me
as the sentimental type.


00:57:54.655 --> 00:57:55.808
Secondly,


00:57:55.928 --> 00:57:57.880
I can't imagine Sweet
Dave liftin' his fat ass


00:57:57.892 --> 00:57:59.981
outta' his chair long
enough to fetch well water,


00:58:00.101 --> 00:58:02.672
unless Minnie was
layin' a fryin' pan upside his head.


00:58:02.792 --> 00:58:05.185
Along takin' trips to the north side.


00:58:05.305 --> 00:58:10.599
That sounds a whole lot like you're calling
me a liar, mi negro amigo.


00:58:11.243 --> 00:58:13.837
Yeah it do sound a whole
lot like, don't it?


00:58:15.238 --> 00:58:16.882
But I still haven't done it yet.


00:58:19.330 --> 00:58:21.167
Minnie still serve food?


00:58:21.957 --> 00:58:24.206
- Do you consider stew food?
- Yes.


00:58:24.218 --> 00:58:25.920
Then we serve food.


00:58:26.029 --> 00:58:29.883
She still stinkin' up the place
with her "Old Quail" pipe tobacco?


00:58:33.912 --> 00:58:36.602
Minnie dosen't smoke a pipe.


00:58:37.021 --> 00:58:39.109
She rolls her own.


00:58:39.229 --> 00:58:41.751
"Red Apple Tobacco"


00:58:41.871 --> 00:58:45.593
But mi negro amigo,
I think you already know this.


00:58:45.713 --> 00:58:48.315
Yeah I do, Senor Bob.


00:58:48.573 --> 00:58:50.861
Just seein' if you do.


00:59:33.063 --> 00:59:36.237
- Fill me up, O.B.
- Yeah.


00:59:36.495 --> 00:59:38.444
Goddamn it!


00:59:40.715 --> 00:59:42.133
Thank you.


00:59:50.125 --> 00:59:53.830
Well cut my legs off and call me Shorty...


00:59:53.950 --> 00:59:57.455
is that Genaral Sanford Smithers I see?


00:59:58.519 --> 01:00:00.671
You've got a good eye son.


01:00:02.176 --> 01:00:04.770
Well, I'll be double dogged damned!


01:00:04.890 --> 01:00:09.387
General Sandy "Don't give a damn" Smithers!


01:00:09.507 --> 01:00:12.423
Captain Chris Mannix, Mannix Marauders.


01:00:12.543 --> 01:00:15.613
- Erskine's boy?
- Yes sir.


01:00:17.241 --> 01:00:18.386
May I sit down, Sir?


01:00:18.398 --> 01:00:21.027
According to the Yankees,
it's a free country.


01:00:22.203 --> 01:00:24.411
Genaral Sandy Smithers...


01:00:25.587 --> 01:00:26.587
boy...


01:00:27.665 --> 01:00:29.067
oh boy.


01:00:29.187 --> 01:00:32.580
Did my daddy talk about you.


01:00:32.700 --> 01:00:36.576
I heard you gave those
Blue Bellies sweet hell.


01:00:37.833 --> 01:00:40.346
Me and my boys did our part.


01:00:40.668 --> 01:00:43.273
Just like Erskine and
his boys did their part.


01:00:43.285 --> 01:00:44.406
Hell yeah, we did.


01:00:44.793 --> 01:00:48.869
- Yankees sons of bitches?
- I never knew your father, son.


01:00:50.046 --> 01:00:54.606
But, I always respected his resolve.


01:00:54.726 --> 01:01:00.132
Thank you for saying that, General. Your
respect woulda' meant the world to him.


01:01:01.708 --> 01:01:03.448
Can I get ya' some coffy?


01:01:04.673 --> 01:01:07.045
- That would be nice.
- Well, how about a blanked?


01:01:09.184 --> 01:01:11.260
That would be even nicer.


01:01:11.621 --> 01:01:14.314
Hell, you know what, you can have mine.


01:01:17.923 --> 01:01:19.251
Here we go General.


01:01:22.692 --> 01:01:26.778
So what brings you out Wyoming way, sir?
If ya' don't mind me askin'?


01:01:26.898 --> 01:01:28.338
My boy.


01:01:28.458 --> 01:01:30.760
You gotta' boy that lives in Red Rock?


01:01:30.880 --> 01:01:35.668
My son, Chester Charles Smithers,


01:01:35.788 --> 01:01:38.249
he died out here a few years back.


01:01:39.229 --> 01:01:41.364
Forgive me sir.


01:01:41.484 --> 01:01:44.948
No forgiveness needed, son.


01:01:45.068 --> 01:01:48.213
Like I said, it was a few years back.


01:01:48.333 --> 01:01:50.958
It was after he served his service.


01:01:52.660 --> 01:01:56.681
He came out here to the hills of Wyoming,


01:01:57.570 --> 01:01:59.285
to make his fortune.


01:02:01.244 --> 01:02:03.164
Never to be heard from again.


01:02:09.610 --> 01:02:12.420
I bought him a symbolic plot


01:02:14.045 --> 01:02:16.107
in the Red Rock cemetery.


01:02:17.216 --> 01:02:21.417
I'm here to advise the stone maker
on his headstone.


01:02:21.740 --> 01:02:24.189
Was he a goner fer' sure?


01:02:24.653 --> 01:02:27.775
No chance he could be livin'
"the cold life" out in


01:02:27.787 --> 01:02:31.041
the woods? It's a rough life,
but folks can learn it.


01:02:31.161 --> 01:02:34.177
If he had done what he came here to do,


01:02:34.435 --> 01:02:36.150
he'd a come home.


01:02:39.243 --> 01:02:40.828
Close it, close it!


01:02:44.618 --> 01:02:47.212
You have to hold it closed
while I nail it shut!


01:02:47.224 --> 01:02:49.829
Really? Who's the idiot
who broke the damn door?


01:02:51.024 --> 01:02:53.112
Fucking hold it low.


01:03:01.185 --> 01:03:02.767
Ok.


01:03:09.754 --> 01:03:11.106
Hold it, mi negro amigo.


01:03:14.393 --> 01:03:16.365
We need two pieces of wood.


01:03:20.167 --> 01:03:21.766
Ola mi cabron.


01:03:22.358 --> 01:03:25.065
There you go, motherfucker!


01:03:29.267 --> 01:03:32.347
That's a lotta' hats, Senor Bob?


01:03:32.467 --> 01:03:35.750
Considering Minnie's no
hats indoors policy? Which,


01:03:35.870 --> 01:03:38.661
If I remember it correctly,
that was one of them Bar of Iron rules,


01:03:38.781 --> 01:03:41.331
kinda rule,
she'd want kept up in her absence.


01:03:41.451 --> 01:03:44.914
You seem to have a laissez faire
attitude when it comes to the hats.


01:03:45.442 --> 01:03:46.706
I'm guilty.


01:03:46.826 --> 01:03:50.044
I have a laissez faire
attitude about the hats.


01:03:50.164 --> 01:03:52.488
How about we forget
about the hats today,


01:03:52.500 --> 01:03:55.226
considering there's a
blizzard going on and all,


01:03:55.346 --> 01:03:58.397
and make tomorrow "No Hat Day"?


01:04:05.215 --> 01:04:07.857
A large black dog.


01:04:11.943 --> 01:04:14.121
Labrador.


01:04:21.791 --> 01:04:25.757
You know my daddy, I said that my daddy!


01:04:25.877 --> 01:04:29.048
Always said that Davis
was a courages man.


01:04:29.168 --> 01:04:34.113
But he should have put capital
in Montgomery and not Richmond.


01:04:34.233 --> 01:04:39.333
Yes, Sir. I agree with that the army in
North Virginia would've been used in a...


01:04:39.453 --> 01:04:43.858
I said the army of North Virginia would
have been used in very different way.


01:04:48.550 --> 01:04:49.839
Shut up!


01:04:56.490 --> 01:04:57.490
O.B.?


01:05:01.002 --> 01:05:03.670
Do you know that nigger, Sir?


01:05:03.992 --> 01:05:06.683
I don't know that nigger.


01:05:06.803 --> 01:05:09.136
But I know he's a nigger.


01:05:09.256 --> 01:05:11.262
And that's all I need to know.


01:05:20.402 --> 01:05:23.817
Well that nigger just ain't any nigger.


01:05:23.937 --> 01:05:26.946
- That nigger is...
- General Sanford Smithers?


01:05:27.066 --> 01:05:29.747
Battle of Baton Rouge?


01:05:32.609 --> 01:05:37.520
Inform the nigger in the
Cavalry officers uniform


01:05:37.640 --> 01:05:42.663
that I had a division
of Confederates under my commend,


01:05:42.783 --> 01:05:43.848
in Baton Rouge.


01:05:43.968 --> 01:05:49.932
Major Nigger, General Smithers wishes me to
inform you... I heard 'em hillbilly.


01:05:50.052 --> 01:05:54.779
Inform this old cracker that
I was in Baton Rouge also.


01:05:55.023 --> 01:05:56.802
On the other side.


01:05:57.769 --> 01:05:59.574
Oh that's interesting.


01:06:00.218 --> 01:06:04.214
General Smithers,
he said that he was also in Baton Rouge.


01:06:04.334 --> 01:06:08.326
- On the other...
- Cap't Mannix, tell the nigger,


01:06:08.446 --> 01:06:12.567
that I don't acknowledge
niggers in Northern uniforms.


01:06:12.687 --> 01:06:15.867
You captured a whole
Colored Command that day.


01:06:15.987 --> 01:06:19.566
But not one Colored Trooper
made it to a camp, did they?


01:06:19.686 --> 01:06:22.260
We had neither the time or the food.


01:06:22.380 --> 01:06:28.162
Nor the inclination
to care for Northern horses,


01:06:28.282 --> 01:06:32.197
and least of all Northern niggers.


01:06:32.317 --> 01:06:36.205
- So we shot 'em where they stood.
- Gentlemen,


01:06:36.325 --> 01:06:38.022
Gentlemen,


01:06:39.775 --> 01:06:42.314
I know Americans aren't apt


01:06:42.434 --> 01:06:47.998
to let a little thing like an unconditional
surrender get in the way of a good war.


01:06:48.118 --> 01:06:52.883
But I strongly suggest we don't restage
The Battle of Baton Rouge,


01:06:53.003 --> 01:06:57.549
during a blizzard
in Minnie's Haberdashery.


01:06:57.669 --> 01:07:01.609
Now, my Nubian friend,


01:07:01.729 --> 01:07:06.520
while I realize passions are high,
that was a while ago.


01:07:06.640 --> 01:07:10.749
And if you shoot this
un-armed old man I guarantee


01:07:10.761 --> 01:07:14.640
I will hang you by the
neck until you are dead.


01:07:14.910 --> 01:07:17.166
Once we arrive in Red Rock.


01:07:20.787 --> 01:07:23.597
I damn will guarantee that too.


01:07:23.717 --> 01:07:26.407
Yeah Warren,
that's the problem with old men.


01:07:26.527 --> 01:07:29.241
You can kick 'em down
the stairs and say it's


01:07:29.253 --> 01:07:31.741
a accident, but ya'
can't just shoot 'em.


01:07:31.861 --> 01:07:36.871
Gentlemen, since we may be trapped here,


01:07:36.991 --> 01:07:41.112
close together like for a few days,


01:07:41.232 --> 01:07:45.687
may I suggest a possible solution?


01:07:45.807 --> 01:07:49.115
We divide Minnie's in half.


01:07:49.235 --> 01:07:53.330
The Northern side and The Southern Side.


01:07:54.052 --> 01:07:56.785
With the dinner table


01:07:56.905 --> 01:08:01.064
operating as a neutral territory.


01:08:01.184 --> 01:08:05.756
We could say that the
fireplace side of the room,


01:08:05.876 --> 01:08:10.924
acts as a symbolic representative of...


01:08:11.044 --> 01:08:12.793
Georgia


01:08:14.082 --> 01:08:18.426
While the bar, represents...


01:08:21.660 --> 01:08:24.032
Philadelphia!


01:08:24.152 --> 01:08:28.040
As long aas the bar's Philadelphia I agree.


01:08:36.767 --> 01:08:40.131
We still got that deal
we talked about in the wagon?


01:08:40.530 --> 01:08:45.879
I help you protect your eight thousand,
you help me protect my ten?


01:08:47.156 --> 01:08:52.337
One of them fella's
is not what he says he is.


01:08:52.582 --> 01:08:54.270
What is he?


01:08:54.390 --> 01:08:57.583
He's in cahoots with this one
that's what he is.


01:08:57.703 --> 01:09:03.499
One of them, maybe even two of 'em,
is here to see Domergue goes free.


01:09:03.619 --> 01:09:08.371
And to accomplish that goal,
they'll kill everbody in here.


01:09:08.491 --> 01:09:12.129
And they got 'em coupla' days.
So all they gotta' do


01:09:12.141 --> 01:09:15.654
is sit tight and wait for
a winda' of opportunity.


01:09:15.774 --> 01:09:18.902
And that's when they strike,


01:09:20.281 --> 01:09:22.008
huh bitch?


01:09:23.026 --> 01:09:25.733
If you say so, John.


01:09:27.486 --> 01:09:30.060
Are you sure you're not
just being paranoid?


01:09:30.072 --> 01:09:31.392
Our best bet is this,


01:09:31.512 --> 01:09:35.633
duplicitous fella' ain't
as cool a customer as Daisy here.


01:09:35.753 --> 01:09:41.149
He won't have the leather patience
it takes to just sit here and wait.


01:09:41.269 --> 01:09:47.039
But waiting for an oportunity, and knowing
it's the right one, isn't so easy.


01:09:47.159 --> 01:09:50.829
If he can't handle it, he'll stop waiting.


01:09:50.949 --> 01:09:56.436
He'll try and create his opportunity.
And that's when Mr.Jumpy reveals himself.


01:09:56.797 --> 01:09:59.065
And what do you got to say about all this?


01:09:59.361 --> 01:10:03.202
What do I got to say?
About John Ruth's ravings?


01:10:03.847 --> 01:10:07.469
He's absolutely right.


01:10:07.589 --> 01:10:11.319
Me and one of them fella's
is in cahoots. And


01:10:11.331 --> 01:10:15.073
we're just waitin' for
everybody go to sleep.


01:10:15.193 --> 01:10:19.211
That's when we gonna' kill y'all.


01:10:19.662 --> 01:10:22.665
Ok everybody,


01:10:25.239 --> 01:10:27.822
hear this.


01:10:29.459 --> 01:10:32.153
This here is Daisy Domergue.


01:10:32.939 --> 01:10:35.814
She's wanted dead or alive for murder.


01:10:35.934 --> 01:10:38.688
Ten thousand dollars.


01:10:38.808 --> 01:10:41.923
That money's mine boys.


01:10:42.043 --> 01:10:44.488
Don't wanna' share it.


01:10:44.608 --> 01:10:47.526
I ain't gonna' lose it.


01:10:47.646 --> 01:10:53.704
When the sun comes out, I'm taking
this woman into Red Rock, to hang.


01:10:59.401 --> 01:11:00.974
Now...


01:11:04.389 --> 01:11:07.599
is there anybody here...


01:11:07.719 --> 01:11:10.692
comitted to stopping me'...


01:11:10.812 --> 01:11:13.296
from doing that?


01:11:23.170 --> 01:11:25.271
Really?


01:11:25.391 --> 01:11:27.874
Nobody gotta' problem with this?


01:11:33.185 --> 01:11:38.431
Well, I guess that's
very fortunate for me.


01:11:38.551 --> 01:11:43.677
However, I hope you all understand,


01:11:43.797 --> 01:11:47.801
I can't just take your word.


01:11:47.921 --> 01:11:52.996
Circumstances force me to, take...


01:11:53.116 --> 01:11:55.974
precautions.


01:11:56.094 --> 01:12:00.726
When you say precautions...


01:12:00.846 --> 01:12:04.468
why do I feel you mean me?


01:12:04.588 --> 01:12:07.586
Because I'm gonna' take your gun, son.


01:12:07.598 --> 01:12:09.649
- You are?
- Yes I am.


01:12:09.758 --> 01:12:13.491
- Nothing personal.
- Just mine?


01:12:13.611 --> 01:12:16.105
The Hangman got himself a gun too?


01:12:16.117 --> 01:12:19.910
I'll be dealing with his
gun after I deal with yours.


01:12:27.024 --> 01:12:30.788
I feel kinda' naked without it.


01:12:30.908 --> 01:12:34.242
Oh, I still got mine.


01:12:35.918 --> 01:12:38.637
I'll protect you.


01:12:46.036 --> 01:12:50.432
A bastards work is never
done, huh, John Ruth?


01:12:50.767 --> 01:12:53.899
That's right, Joe Gage.


01:12:54.019 --> 01:12:57.443
- Now gimmie the gun.
- You want it?


01:12:57.563 --> 01:13:00.433
You have to come and take...


01:13:01.567 --> 01:13:04.390
Calm down.


01:13:05.099 --> 01:13:08.527
Take your hand away from your gun.


01:13:11.375 --> 01:13:14.507
Blink if you're calm.


01:13:14.739 --> 01:13:17.536
- Did he blink?
- He blinked.


01:13:17.656 --> 01:13:21.351
Blink if your gonna' remain calm?


01:13:23.916 --> 01:13:27.873
- He blinked.
- Take his pistol.


01:13:29.330 --> 01:13:33.412
I'm real sorry about this, son.


01:13:33.532 --> 01:13:39.151
Like I said, nothing personal.
Just a precaution.


01:14:25.320 --> 01:14:26.802
Pretty sneaky.


01:15:01.849 --> 01:15:05.587
I'm afraid the same
applies to you too, Mr.


01:15:05.707 --> 01:15:07.095
Mobray.


01:15:07.215 --> 01:15:12.547
Precautions must be taken
because life is too sweet to lose.


01:15:16.904 --> 01:15:19.353
Hand me that little bucket.


01:15:29.432 --> 01:15:30.721
O.B.?


01:15:32.481 --> 01:15:34.252
Go to the outhouse.


01:15:34.935 --> 01:15:39.421
Take this bucket and dump
it down the shit hole.


01:15:40.826 --> 01:15:42.945
Why do I gotta' go outside?


01:15:42.957 --> 01:15:47.219
Your jacket's already on.
And I sorta kinda trust you.


01:16:26.363 --> 01:16:28.387
After you Major.


01:16:45.530 --> 01:16:46.961
Ok.


01:16:48.765 --> 01:16:51.807
I'm gonna' cut you loose while we eat.


01:16:52.129 --> 01:16:54.797
Don't get any ideas,
I ain't goin' soft on ya'.


01:16:56.047 --> 01:16:59.039
You lift your ass even
one inch off this seat,


01:16:59.051 --> 01:17:02.118
I'll put a bullet right
in your goddamn throat.


01:17:26.584 --> 01:17:29.046
So Domergue,


01:17:29.329 --> 01:17:34.201
I suppose this blizzard counts as a stroke
of luck as far as you're concerned?


01:17:34.459 --> 01:17:38.351
- You don't hear me complaining do ya'?
- No I sure don't.


01:17:46.317 --> 01:17:49.385
How 'bout you Oswaldo?


01:17:50.571 --> 01:17:52.247
How about me what?


01:17:52.367 --> 01:17:54.051
Look,


01:17:54.171 --> 01:17:57.146
considerin' all the thing I done
for money, I ain't one to judge.


01:17:57.266 --> 01:18:02.945
But don't you feel just the least
little bad 'bout hangin' a woman?


01:18:03.065 --> 01:18:06.367
Till they invent a trigger
a woman can't pull, if


01:18:06.379 --> 01:18:09.494
you're a hang man, you're
going to hang woman.


01:18:09.614 --> 01:18:12.587
Well hell Ozzy, I guess I ain't never
looked at it like that before.


01:18:12.707 --> 01:18:15.134
When it comes to some
of them mean bastards


01:18:15.146 --> 01:18:17.640
out therem it's the only
thing does the job.


01:18:17.760 --> 01:18:23.736
You really only need to hang mean bastards.
But mean bastards, you need to hang.


01:18:32.527 --> 01:18:34.988
You goddamn son of a bitch!


01:18:35.903 --> 01:18:38.545
I almost died out there!


01:18:41.729 --> 01:18:47.851
I ain't never going out in that shit
ever, ever again!


01:19:10.549 --> 01:19:12.082
You ok, O.B.?


01:19:12.202 --> 01:19:13.797
I'm fine.


01:19:13.917 --> 01:19:15.717
I'll be fine.


01:19:15.837 --> 01:19:18.463
I just need to get warm.


01:19:23.386 --> 01:19:25.461
You want some stew, O.B.?


01:19:25.581 --> 01:19:28.400
Stew, later.


01:19:34.290 --> 01:19:35.759
That's nice.


01:20:00.198 --> 01:20:01.268
So...


01:20:02.402 --> 01:20:04.026
how you doin', black Major?


01:20:04.146 --> 01:20:09.693
I ain't in the mood, Chris Mannix.
Leave me be from your horseshit.


01:20:09.813 --> 01:20:11.669
John Ruth says you gotta' a Lincoln Letter?


01:20:11.789 --> 01:20:15.066
I tole' you jackass to
Hee-Haw somewhere else.


01:20:15.078 --> 01:20:16.554
That's right, John.


01:20:16.674 --> 01:20:20.601
- You did say, didn't ya'?
- Yeah I did.


01:20:21.813 --> 01:20:23.321
So...


01:20:24.932 --> 01:20:28.748
- you got a letter from Abraham Lincoln?
- Yes.


01:20:29.044 --> 01:20:32.138
Thee Abraham Lincoln?


01:20:32.258 --> 01:20:33.531
Yes.


01:20:33.543 --> 01:20:37.396
Abraham Lincoln The President
of the United States...


01:20:37.654 --> 01:20:39.842
- Yes.
- Of America?


01:20:39.854 --> 01:20:41.068
Yes.


01:20:41.177 --> 01:20:45.620
- Wrote you a letter, personally?
- Yes.


01:20:45.740 --> 01:20:50.595
- Personally? As in: "Dear Maj. Warren"?
- No. Personally as in: "Dear Marquis".


01:20:50.715 --> 01:20:55.466
"Dear Marquis" Abraham Lincoln the
President of the United States of America?


01:20:55.478 --> 01:20:57.066
Yes.


01:20:57.186 --> 01:21:00.546
- May I see it?
- No you may not.


01:21:00.666 --> 01:21:03.810
But the way John tells it,
you weren't just some


01:21:03.822 --> 01:21:07.235
random nigger soldier picked
from a pile of letters.


01:21:07.355 --> 01:21:09.426
Way John tells it,


01:21:09.697 --> 01:21:13.409
- y'all hada' correspondence.
- Yes.


01:21:13.847 --> 01:21:18.913
Way John tells it, y'all's
practically pen pals?


01:21:20.086 --> 01:21:21.086
Yes.


01:21:22.586 --> 01:21:24.881
And a pen pal's...


01:21:25.319 --> 01:21:28.064
practically a friend.


01:21:38.802 --> 01:21:40.929
John Ruth,


01:21:41.049 --> 01:21:43.778
you really think a nigger
drummed outta' the


01:21:43.790 --> 01:21:46.471
Calvary with a yellow
stripe down his back,


01:21:46.591 --> 01:21:50.312
was practically friends with The President
of The United States of America?


01:21:54.153 --> 01:21:58.903
John Ruth, I hate to be the one to break it
to ya' but nobody in Minnie's Haberdashery,


01:21:59.023 --> 01:22:02.119
had ever corresponded with Abraham Lincoln,


01:22:02.239 --> 01:22:05.869
Least of all, that nigger there.


01:22:15.484 --> 01:22:18.036
Was all that horseshit?


01:22:20.737 --> 01:22:23.863
Course it was.


01:22:48.737 --> 01:22:51.869
Well I guess it's true
what they say about you people.


01:22:54.498 --> 01:22:58.120
You can't trust a fuckin' word
that comes outta' your mouth.


01:22:59.319 --> 01:23:01.858
What's the matter, John Ruth?


01:23:01.978 --> 01:23:04.242
I hurt your feelings?


01:23:04.362 --> 01:23:07.774
As a matter of fact, you did.


01:23:11.293 --> 01:23:12.917
I know,


01:23:13.037 --> 01:23:17.879
I'm the only black son of a bitch you ever
met, so I'm gonna' cut you some slack.


01:23:17.999 --> 01:23:23.073
But you got no idea, what it's like
being a black man facin' down America.


01:23:23.861 --> 01:23:26.141
The only time black folks are safe,


01:23:26.261 --> 01:23:29.751
is when white folks is disarmed.
And this letter,


01:23:29.871 --> 01:23:34.674
had the desired effect of
disarming white folks.


01:23:36.840 --> 01:23:38.787
Call it what you want,


01:23:40.577 --> 01:23:43.710
I call it a dirty fuckin' trick.


01:23:52.590 --> 01:23:56.392
You wanna' know why I'd lie
about something like that, white man?


01:24:01.974 --> 01:24:04.784
Got me on that stagecoach, didn't it.


01:24:11.731 --> 01:24:14.631
Well I'll tell you like
the lord tole' John,


01:24:14.751 --> 01:24:18.975
a letter from Abraham Lincoln wouldn't
have that kinda' effect on me.


01:24:19.095 --> 01:24:22.584
- I might let a whore piss on it.
- I spit on it.


01:24:22.704 --> 01:24:25.381
Good for you, sister.


01:24:41.040 --> 01:24:45.534
Warren goddamit,
you leave that old man alone!


01:24:45.654 --> 01:24:50.333
Stand down you son of a bitch,
I shared a battle field with this man.


01:24:50.453 --> 01:24:52.911
Or would you deny me that too?


01:24:56.713 --> 01:24:59.459
I suppose you were there.


01:25:00.362 --> 01:25:02.553
May I join you?


01:25:06.201 --> 01:25:08.470
Yes you may.


01:25:58.377 --> 01:25:59.498
Damn it.


01:26:05.724 --> 01:26:06.755
So,


01:26:07.038 --> 01:26:09.152
how's life since the war?


01:26:14.565 --> 01:26:16.950
Got both my legs.


01:26:17.070 --> 01:26:20.198
Got both my arms.


01:26:20.624 --> 01:26:24.890
- I can't complain.
- Got a woman?


01:26:26.785 --> 01:26:30.136
Fever took her, started this last winter.


01:26:31.012 --> 01:26:32.907
What was her name?


01:26:33.680 --> 01:26:36.916
- Betsy.
- Georgia girl?


01:26:38.398 --> 01:26:40.151
Augusta.


01:26:41.362 --> 01:26:44.520
Atlanta boy, and a Augusta girl.


01:26:46.015 --> 01:26:48.838
I use to raise Kentucky horses.


01:26:48.958 --> 01:26:54.033
Her paw' was the owner of the breedershit
where I brought of my ponies.


01:26:56.302 --> 01:26:57.578
God damnit.


01:26:58.080 --> 01:27:00.710
I made good deal on her.


01:27:01.277 --> 01:27:05.092
Took the stake he gave and
bought a bunch peach ochards.


01:27:05.402 --> 01:27:07.477
Set myself up pretty well.


01:27:08.005 --> 01:27:12.465
Did a hellva' lot better than
my no good brothers, that's for damn sure.


01:27:14.965 --> 01:27:18.562
Yeah, your son came up
here a few years back.


01:27:18.871 --> 01:27:21.513
He spoke highly of his mama too.


01:27:22.609 --> 01:27:26.952
You knew my boy?


01:27:27.815 --> 01:27:29.208
Yeah...


01:27:30.651 --> 01:27:33.010
Yeah I knew 'em.


01:27:33.130 --> 01:27:35.472
You did not know my boy.


01:27:39.170 --> 01:27:41.826
Suit yourself.


01:27:43.269 --> 01:27:46.375
Didja' know my son?


01:27:46.633 --> 01:27:51.995
- I know the day he died... do you?
- No.


01:27:52.115 --> 01:27:55.179
You wanna know what day that was?


01:27:59.277 --> 01:28:04.201
The day he met me.


01:28:19.565 --> 01:28:22.968
He came up here to
do a little nigger head huntin'.


01:28:23.088 --> 01:28:28.627
By then the reward was so,
five thousand and bragging rights.


01:28:28.747 --> 01:28:33.576
But back then to battle hard rebs, five
thousand just to cut off a niggers head,


01:28:34.764 --> 01:28:37.611
now that's good money.


01:28:37.731 --> 01:28:42.908
So the Johnny's climbed this mountain,
lookin' for fortune.


01:28:43.720 --> 01:28:47.045
But there was no fortune to be found.


01:28:47.806 --> 01:28:51.493
All they found was me.


01:28:53.285 --> 01:28:56.268
All them fella's came up
here sang a different tune,


01:28:56.388 --> 01:29:00.392
when they found
themselves at the mercy of a nigger's gun,


01:29:03.055 --> 01:29:07.888
"Let's just forget it.
I go my way, you go yours"


01:29:08.198 --> 01:29:12.567
- that's your boy Chester talkin'
- You a goddamn lie.


01:29:12.687 --> 01:29:16.586
"If you just let me
home to my family, I'll


01:29:16.598 --> 01:29:20.687
swear, I'll never set
foot in Wyoming again."


01:29:22.762 --> 01:29:26.204
That's what they all said.


01:29:28.266 --> 01:29:30.741
Beggin' for his life.


01:29:30.861 --> 01:29:36.657
Your boy told me his whole life story.


01:29:38.848 --> 01:29:42.727
And you was in that story, General.


01:29:43.771 --> 01:29:47.883
And when I knew me I had the son.


01:29:48.003 --> 01:29:52.983
Of The Bloody Nigger
Killer of Baton Rouge...


01:29:53.103 --> 01:29:58.259
- I knew me I was gonna' have some fun.
- You shut your lyin' nigger lips up!


01:29:58.379 --> 01:30:02.435
General Smithers, don't you listen to him,
he didn't know your boy!


01:30:02.555 --> 01:30:05.631
He just heard, tell why you here is all!


01:30:05.751 --> 01:30:09.459
It was cold the day I killed your boy.


01:30:09.579 --> 01:30:15.681
And I don't mean snwoy mountain in
Wyoming cold. It was colder than that.


01:30:15.801 --> 01:30:18.108
And on that cold day,


01:30:18.228 --> 01:30:22.955
with your boy at the
business end of my gun barrel...


01:30:23.075 --> 01:30:25.314
I made him strip.


01:30:25.434 --> 01:30:29.786
Right down to his bare ass.


01:30:31.036 --> 01:30:34.452
Then I told him to start walkin'.


01:31:02.434 --> 01:31:07.100
I walked his naked ass for two hours,
'fore his cold collapsed him.


01:31:09.381 --> 01:31:13.441
- You never even knew my boy?
- No he didn't!


01:31:13.561 --> 01:31:18.013
He's just a sneaky nigger
tryin' to getcha to go for that gun!


01:31:18.133 --> 01:31:21.587
Then he commits to begging again.


01:31:21.707 --> 01:31:26.099
But this time he wasn't begging to go home.


01:31:26.408 --> 01:31:31.138
He knew he'd never see his home again.
And he wasn't beggin' for his life neither.


01:31:31.258 --> 01:31:34.787
'Cos he knew that was long gone.


01:31:34.907 --> 01:31:40.522
All he wanted... was a blanket.


01:31:40.642 --> 01:31:44.386
Now don't judge your boy
too harshly, General. You


01:31:44.398 --> 01:31:47.934
ain't never been cold as
your boy was that day.


01:31:49.739 --> 01:31:57.382
You'd be surprised what a man that cold,
would do for a blanket.


01:31:58.864 --> 01:32:01.429
Wanna know what your boy did?


01:32:03.581 --> 01:32:08.569
I took my big, black,
pecker outta' my pants.


01:32:09.626 --> 01:32:14.821
And I made him crawl through
the snow on all fours over to it.


01:32:23.263 --> 01:32:28.406
Then I grabbed a hand full
of that black hair on the back his head...


01:32:30.210 --> 01:32:38.047
Then I stuck my big, black Johnson
right down his goddamn throat.


01:32:39.065 --> 01:32:41.888
And it was fulla' blood, so it was warm.


01:32:43.267 --> 01:32:47.328
You bet your sweet ass it was warm.


01:32:47.448 --> 01:32:50.937
And Chester Charles Smithers,


01:32:51.057 --> 01:32:57.639
sucked on that warm black dingus
for long as he could.


01:33:08.800 --> 01:33:11.146
Starting to see pictures, ain't ya'?


01:33:11.266 --> 01:33:12.964
Your boy...


01:33:13.084 --> 01:33:15.348
black dudes dingus in his mouth.


01:33:15.468 --> 01:33:19.009
Him shakin', him cryin'


01:33:19.129 --> 01:33:22.786
me laughin'


01:33:24.552 --> 01:33:27.903
and him not understandin'


01:33:29.979 --> 01:33:32.930
But you understand, doncha' Sandy?


01:33:33.050 --> 01:33:35.920
I never did give your boy that blanket.


01:33:36.178 --> 01:33:43.419
Even after all he did,
and he did everything I asked.


01:33:44.775 --> 01:33:46.128
No blanket.


01:33:47.572 --> 01:33:51.581
That blanket was just
a heart breakin' liar's promise.


01:33:51.701 --> 01:33:55.370
Kinda' like those uniforms
the union issued those colored troopers,


01:33:55.490 --> 01:33:59.211
that you chose not to acknowledge.


01:34:05.526 --> 01:34:08.014
So what you gonna' do old man?


01:34:09.547 --> 01:34:12.744
You gonna' spend the
next two or three days,


01:34:12.864 --> 01:34:16.916
ignore the nigger that killed your boy,


01:34:17.036 --> 01:34:21.118
Ignoring how I made him suffer?


01:34:21.238 --> 01:34:24.421
Ignoring how I made him...


01:34:24.898 --> 01:34:29.654
lick, all over my Johnson?


01:34:30.904 --> 01:34:34.655
The dumbest thing your boy ever did...


01:34:34.775 --> 01:34:40.056
was to let me know...
he was your boy.


01:35:08.128 --> 01:35:13.568
Chapter Four
Domergue's Got a Secret


01:35:20.729 --> 01:35:24.753
About fifteen minutes has passed,
since we last left our characters.


01:35:25.344 --> 01:35:29.361
Joe Gag volunteered
to take Smithers dead body outside.


01:35:29.481 --> 01:35:32.326
Straws we drawn to see
who would help him...


01:35:32.446 --> 01:35:35.406
O.B. lost.


01:35:35.526 --> 01:35:36.746
Chris, John Ruth and Oswaldo,


01:35:36.866 --> 01:35:42.322
had vigorous debate about the legality of
self-defense murder they just transpired.


01:35:42.442 --> 01:35:45.116
Marquis Warren who is
supremely confident about the


01:35:45.128 --> 01:35:47.555
legality of what just
transpired, ignored them


01:35:47.675 --> 01:35:50.794
sat at a table by himself
and drank brandy.


01:35:53.524 --> 01:35:56.180
Captain Chris Mannix dawn
the dead Generals coat and


01:35:56.192 --> 01:35:58.860
joined Oswaldo in lighting
the candles and lanterns.


01:35:58.980 --> 01:36:03.031
Hey Ozzy, hey you got the right idea.


01:36:03.151 --> 01:36:05.608
Let's light this place up.


01:36:05.728 --> 01:36:10.271
John Ruth held the door close,
waiting for Joe Gage and O.B. to return.


01:36:14.832 --> 01:36:18.377
Bob enjoyed an manzana roja.


01:36:23.593 --> 01:36:25.587
Domergue, however,


01:36:25.707 --> 01:36:29.816
hasn't moved from her spot at the community
dinner table since John Ruth uncuffed her.


01:36:29.936 --> 01:36:31.054
John Ruth...


01:36:32.434 --> 01:36:33.515
Yeah?


01:36:34.548 --> 01:36:36.764
Can I play that guitar over there?


01:36:37.510 --> 01:36:38.992
Let's go back a bit.


01:36:39.544 --> 01:36:43.250
Your boy, black dudes dingus in his mouth.


01:36:43.370 --> 01:36:48.325
Fifteen minutes ago Major Warren shot
General Smithers in front of everybody.


01:36:48.445 --> 01:36:51.831
But fourty seconds before
that, something equally


01:36:51.843 --> 01:36:55.173
as important happened, but
not everybody saw it.


01:36:55.293 --> 01:36:58.060
While Major Warren was
captivating the crowd


01:36:58.072 --> 01:37:00.912
with tales of black dicks
and white mouths...


01:37:01.032 --> 01:37:05.121
somebody... poisoned the coffy.


01:37:05.241 --> 01:37:10.001
He did everything I asked, no blanket.


01:37:11.445 --> 01:37:14.694
And the only one to see 'em do it...


01:37:18.635 --> 01:37:20.598
was Domergue.


01:37:25.442 --> 01:37:28.866
That's why this chapter is called...


01:37:28.986 --> 01:37:31.564
Domergue's Got a Secret.


01:37:34.284 --> 01:37:36.205
John Ruth.


01:37:36.761 --> 01:37:38.091
Yeah.


01:37:38.856 --> 01:37:41.587
Can I play that guitar over there?


01:37:47.213 --> 01:37:48.245
Yeah.


01:37:54.584 --> 01:37:57.484
You come back with anything
else but a guitar.


01:37:57.604 --> 01:38:00.263
My pistol plays a tune.


01:38:00.383 --> 01:38:04.351
Domergues death march, you got it?


01:38:04.471 --> 01:38:08.259
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I got it.


01:41:03.632 --> 01:41:07.989
That's the one you like to sing
in the stagecoach, huh?


01:41:08.109 --> 01:41:09.277
Yeah.


01:41:09.397 --> 01:41:11.559
It's kinda' pretty.


01:41:12.229 --> 01:41:15.684
- Got another verse to it?
- Yeah I got.


01:41:18.685 --> 01:41:20.524
Go ahead, sing it.


01:42:07.558 --> 01:42:09.704
Gimme that guitar!


01:42:12.468 --> 01:42:14.254
Music time's over!


01:42:18.888 --> 01:42:20.713
Turn around.


01:42:28.136 --> 01:42:31.660
- No, no, no, no, no.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, shut up!


01:44:16.609 --> 01:44:20.215
When you get to hell, John.


01:44:20.335 --> 01:44:22.872
Tell 'em Daisy sent ya'.


01:44:35.924 --> 01:44:38.783
Mannix the coffy!


01:45:32.959 --> 01:45:34.429
Oh my god!


01:45:38.115 --> 01:45:40.249
Gimme that fucking gun!


01:45:41.095 --> 01:45:43.754
Don't test me, bitch.


01:45:46.473 --> 01:45:51.750
Everybody get your back sides up
against that back wall over yonder.


01:45:51.870 --> 01:45:54.388
Goddamit...


01:45:54.508 --> 01:45:57.368
Get or don't get, Joe Gage.
It's up to you.


01:45:57.488 --> 01:45:59.820
- I'll get.
- Then get.


01:46:12.364 --> 01:46:14.809
You too, Senor Bob.


01:46:19.815 --> 01:46:22.997
Everybody turn around
and put your hands on that wall.


01:46:26.884 --> 01:46:29.160
Move 'em down snowshoes.


01:46:50.066 --> 01:46:54.094
Everybody keep your mouth
shut and do like I say.


01:46:54.214 --> 01:46:57.517
You open your mouth...
you gonna' get a bullet.


01:46:57.637 --> 01:47:00.978
You move a little sudden,
a little strange...


01:47:00.990 --> 01:47:02.805
you gonna' get a bullet.


01:47:02.914 --> 01:47:06.077
Not a warning, not a question...


01:47:06.089 --> 01:47:07.175
a bullet.


01:47:07.284 --> 01:47:09.561
You got that?


01:47:09.681 --> 01:47:11.776
- Let me hear you say, "I got it".
- "I got it."


01:47:11.896 --> 01:47:12.664
"I got it."


01:47:12.676 --> 01:47:13.851
"I got it."


01:47:13.863 --> 01:47:15.247
We have it.


01:47:16.791 --> 01:47:20.476
Chris Mannix,
come over here on this side.


01:47:20.596 --> 01:47:22.289
Come on.


01:47:27.587 --> 01:47:30.123
Take this gun out of my holster.


01:47:40.012 --> 01:47:41.764
Point it at them.


01:47:44.065 --> 01:47:49.889
Like I said, anybody does anything.
And I mean, anything.


01:47:51.370 --> 01:47:52.457
Kill 'em.


01:47:56.385 --> 01:47:58.249
So...


01:47:58.369 --> 01:48:04.038
you finally decided I'm tellin' the truth
'bout bein' the sheriff of Red Rock, huh?


01:48:04.158 --> 01:48:06.253
I don't know 'bout all that.


01:48:06.373 --> 01:48:09.245
But you ain't the killer
who poisoned that coffy.


01:48:09.257 --> 01:48:11.852
'cos you almost drunk
it your own damn self.


01:48:11.972 --> 01:48:15.155
But one of 'em is.


01:48:21.356 --> 01:48:22.577
Gimme the key.


01:48:22.697 --> 01:48:24.701
Gimme the key!


01:48:36.703 --> 01:48:39.986
You motherfucking black bastard!


01:48:40.106 --> 01:48:44.966
You're gonna' die on this mountain
and I'm gonna' fucking laugh when you do!


01:48:47.175 --> 01:48:48.712
What I say 'bout talkin?


01:48:49.821 --> 01:48:51.909
'Meant it, didn't I?


01:48:53.018 --> 01:48:56.616
And you need to understand,
you just killed the only


01:48:56.628 --> 01:49:00.237
man here, comitted to gettin'
you to Red Rock alive.


01:49:05.966 --> 01:49:11.122
Now, one of y'all...
is workin' with her.


01:49:11.242 --> 01:49:14.062
Or two of y'all is workin' with her.


01:49:14.182 --> 01:49:16.372
Or all y'all is...


01:49:18.979 --> 01:49:22.046
but only one of you poisoned the coffy.


01:49:25.884 --> 01:49:31.906
So what charms this bitch got,
take a man brave a blizzard,


01:49:32.026 --> 01:49:39.146
kill in cold blood, I'm
sure I don't know.


01:49:41.372 --> 01:49:44.655
But John Ruth's trying to hang your woman.


01:49:44.775 --> 01:49:50.595
So you kill him... maybe.


01:49:50.715 --> 01:49:53.717
But O.B. wasn't hangin' nobody.


01:49:53.837 --> 01:49:55.193
He damn sure would.


01:49:55.313 --> 01:49:57.523
But he sure enough led over there
dead now, though, ain't he?


01:49:57.643 --> 01:49:59.953
He damn sure is you sons of bitches.


01:49:59.965 --> 01:50:02.941
Just like any one of us
who'd drank that coffy.


01:50:03.061 --> 01:50:06.365
Like me god damnit.


01:50:06.485 --> 01:50:09.922
Now those of y'all with
your hands on the wall


01:50:09.934 --> 01:50:13.677
don't practice in poison
need to think about that.


01:50:13.797 --> 01:50:18.026
Think about how that coulda' you
been you rollin' around on this floor.


01:50:18.146 --> 01:50:21.651
And about the men standin' next
ta' ya' would be responsible.


01:50:21.771 --> 01:50:29.203
And I know who I got my money on. Yeah
that's right Joe Gage I'm lookin' at you.


01:50:30.592 --> 01:50:35.224
Not so fast Chris.
We'll get there.


01:50:35.344 --> 01:50:38.427
Let's slow it down.


01:50:38.547 --> 01:50:41.528
Let's slow it way down.


01:50:46.725 --> 01:50:48.819
Who made the coffy?


01:50:48.939 --> 01:50:50.488
He did.


01:50:52.263 --> 01:50:56.673
- Yeah, he did, didn't he?
- Yeah, he did, didn't he?


01:50:56.793 --> 01:51:01.607
But it's the stew that's got me thinking.


01:51:01.727 --> 01:51:04.670
How long you say Minnie been gone?


01:51:04.790 --> 01:51:06.681
A week?


01:51:07.267 --> 01:51:09.261
Si.


01:51:09.381 --> 01:51:14.477
See, my mama used to make stew.


01:51:14.597 --> 01:51:18.083
And it always tasted the same,
no matter the meat.


01:51:18.203 --> 01:51:21.365
And there was another fellow
on the plantation, Uncle Charly.


01:51:21.485 --> 01:51:25.051
He made stew too and like my mama's.


01:51:25.171 --> 01:51:29.340
I ate his stew from the
time I was a whipper,


01:51:29.460 --> 01:51:33.066
to I was a full grown man.


01:51:33.186 --> 01:51:38.846
And no matter the meat,
it always tasted like Uncle Charly's stew.


01:51:38.966 --> 01:51:44.706
Now I ain't had Minnie's stew in six
months, so I ain't no expert, but that,


01:51:44.826 --> 01:51:50.004
damn sure is Minnie's stew.


01:51:50.124 --> 01:51:54.998
So if Minnie's on the north side
visiting her mama for a week,


01:51:55.118 --> 01:51:59.651
how'd she make the stew this morning?


01:52:02.268 --> 01:52:04.322
And this?


01:52:04.625 --> 01:52:08.914
This... is Sweet Dave's chair.


01:52:09.034 --> 01:52:12.579
When I sat in it earlier,
I couldn't belive it.


01:52:12.699 --> 01:52:15.681
Nobody sits in Sweet Dave's chaire.


01:52:15.801 --> 01:52:21.239
This may be Minnie's place,
but this is damn sure,


01:52:21.359 --> 01:52:24.663
Sweet Dave's chair.


01:52:25.590 --> 01:52:30.444
And if... he went to
the north side....


01:52:30.746 --> 01:52:37.956
I'm pretty goddamn sure
that chair's be going with him.


01:52:40.010 --> 01:52:41.984
What's in the chair?


01:52:42.104 --> 01:52:44.481
Just what I thought.


01:52:44.601 --> 01:52:47.884
Sweet Dave's goddamn blood.


01:52:53.142 --> 01:52:54.894
So...


01:52:55.014 --> 01:52:58.519
are you actually accusing me of murder?


01:53:01.116 --> 01:53:04.057
The way I see it, Senior Bob,


01:53:04.177 --> 01:53:07.420
whoever's workin' with her,


01:53:07.540 --> 01:53:11.972
ain't who they say they is.
And if it's you,


01:53:12.092 --> 01:53:16.040
that means Minnie
and her man ain't at her mama's.


01:53:16.160 --> 01:53:19.746
They're lyin' out back
there dead somewhere.


01:53:19.866 --> 01:53:22.042
Or if it's you Britisch Man,


01:53:22.162 --> 01:53:24.968
the real Oswaldo Mobray is lyin'
in a ditch somewhere. And


01:53:24.980 --> 01:53:27.560
you're just an English fella'
passin' off his papers.


01:53:27.680 --> 01:53:33.643
Or we go by my theory, which
is the ugliest guy did it.


01:53:33.763 --> 01:53:37.147
Which makes it you, Joe Gage.


01:53:37.267 --> 01:53:40.743
So I take it you've
deduced the coffy was


01:53:40.755 --> 01:53:44.659
poisoned while you were
murdering the old man?


01:53:44.779 --> 01:53:46.471
Yes.


01:53:46.591 --> 01:53:51.184
Well, mi negro amigo,
during that whole incident...


01:53:51.304 --> 01:53:55.997
I was sitting on that side of the room.
Playing Silent Night on the piano.


01:53:56.117 --> 01:54:02.683
I didn't say you poisoned the coffy.
I said you didn't make the stew.


01:54:03.630 --> 01:54:06.671
My theory is...


01:54:06.791 --> 01:54:11.827
you're working with man
who poisoned the coffy.


01:54:11.947 --> 01:54:14.434
And both of y'all murdered Minnie,


01:54:14.554 --> 01:54:17.552
and Sweet Dave and whoever
else picked this bad luck


01:54:17.564 --> 01:54:20.346
day to visit Minnie's
Haberdashery this morning.


01:54:20.466 --> 01:54:28.466
And at some point, y'all intented
to bushwhack John Ruth and free Daisy.


01:54:29.951 --> 01:54:37.951
But you didn't count on the blizzard
and you didn't count on the two of us.


01:54:40.284 --> 01:54:42.781
That's as far as I got.
How am I doin'?


01:54:45.943 --> 01:54:50.796
Your a real imaginative nigger, ain't you?


01:54:50.916 --> 01:54:56.475
So, do you intend to murder me
based on a far fetched nigger theory?


01:54:56.595 --> 01:54:57.966
Or can you prove it, cabrone?


01:55:00.463 --> 01:55:05.135
It ain't so far fetched, Senior Bob.


01:55:05.255 --> 01:55:09.506
And it's a little bit more then my theory.


01:55:12.989 --> 01:55:15.849
How long you say you been
working for Minnie's?


01:55:15.969 --> 01:55:19.051
Four months.


01:55:19.433 --> 01:55:22.463
If you would have been here
two and half years ago


01:55:22.475 --> 01:55:25.576
you'd know about the sign
usta' hang above the bar.


01:55:25.878 --> 01:55:31.578
- Minnie mentioned that to you?
- No.


01:55:32.061 --> 01:55:35.585
You know what that sign said, Senior Bob?


01:55:36.693 --> 01:55:40.177
"No dogs or Mexicans allowed"


01:55:44.245 --> 01:55:47.798
Minnie hung that sign up the
day she opened this Habadashery.


01:55:47.918 --> 01:55:50.908
And it hung over that
Bar every day till she


01:55:50.920 --> 01:55:53.589
took down, a little over two years ago.


01:55:56.368 --> 01:55:59.309
You know why she took it down?


01:55:59.429 --> 01:56:01.967
She started lettin' in dogs.


01:56:05.552 --> 01:56:13.552
Now Minnie likes just about everybody,
but she sure don't like Mexicans.


01:56:14.131 --> 01:56:19.509
So when you tell me, Minnie went
to North side to visit her mama?


01:56:19.629 --> 01:56:25.834
Well I find that highly unlikely...
but... maybe.


01:56:26.136 --> 01:56:30.275
But when you tell me Minnie
Mink took The Habadashery,


01:56:30.287 --> 01:56:34.136
the most precious thing to
her in the whole world,


01:56:36.648 --> 01:56:41.683
and left it in hands of a Goddamn Mexican?


01:56:41.803 --> 01:56:47.987
Well that's what I meant in the barn when I
said: "That sure don't sound like Minnie".


01:56:48.107 --> 01:56:54.552
Now I am calling you a liar, Senior Bob.


01:56:54.672 --> 01:56:59.687
And if you lyin, which you are,


01:56:59.807 --> 01:57:04.343
then you killed Minnie...
and Sweet Dave.


01:57:22.022 --> 01:57:27.319
Four measly bulltes and
there goes Senior, Bob.


01:57:28.628 --> 01:57:31.871
That still don't get us no closer...


01:57:31.991 --> 01:57:35.090
to which one of y'all
poisoned the coffy, though.


01:57:35.210 --> 01:57:38.557
- Does it Chris?
- No it sure don't.


01:57:44.377 --> 01:57:48.626
Now one of y'all poisoned this coffy,
to free Daisy.


01:57:48.746 --> 01:57:51.297
If I don't hear a
confession from one of you


01:57:51.309 --> 01:57:53.701
motherfuckers quick,
fast and in a hurry,


01:57:53.821 --> 01:57:59.219
I'm gonna' pull this whole pot of coffy,
down that bitches goddamn throat.


01:58:00.327 --> 01:58:03.690
